#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wharf — a blueprint built into a ship on Orca (docs/wharf-on-orca-2026-10-17.md S1; B7 of
docs/orchestration-orca-2026-10-15.md, its section 4 Q2 table; the owner's D1-A: under the final words).

    wharf check <blueprint.md> [--plan ID] [--accept] [--json]
        Validate the blueprint (bin/blueprintlib.py) and print its graph; with a plan, say whether
        its digest is the one accepted; --accept records it there.
    wharf apply <blueprint.md> [--plan ID] [--dry-run | --once] [--json]
        The live compile: one Orca Run per ship, a Task per block, a gate per decision block, then
        every row the diff names acted on — ready blocks started, answered gates resolved, ended
        blocks completed — pass after pass until a pass acts on nothing. --once is one pass and
        never the first compile (the tick's form). --dry-run is B6's: the diff, nothing written.
    wharf apply --once --all [--dry-run]
        The tick's (`helm tick`): one pass over every ship with a Run, in every plan on this Mac. On a
        scope's yard, from the tick itself (no session, no dispatched run, no skipper, no ship's
        block: tick_caller()), a ship's `launch: finish` block whose predecessor ended is launched
        (skipper-resilience S6): `autofinish-run <wt> --merge --by ship --digest <the pin's>` when
        plan.json's `merge` says yes, else `--by ship --hold`, at most 2 launches at once in its repo. Off a
        yard, or from any other caller, the block is raised for the skipper as before.
    wharf apply --yard <blueprint.md> [--plan ID] [--no-merge] [--gen N] [--json]
        Lay a ship on its scope's yard (skipper-resilience S2): the blueprint as committed and pushed,
        pinned {repo, branch, rel, digest} and read there from origin/<branch>:<rel>, its text kept in
        the plan (plans/<id>/blueprint-<ship>.md) so the yard's tick drives it with no checkout. On the
        yard it compiles here; elsewhere it runs itself there over the yard's ssh alias
        (wharf-runs/ssh), with the pin and who laid it (`laid_by`: attended or unattended, the depth,
        the session, the host) spelled out, since ssh carries no environment. A pin another plan here
        still drives is refused, naming the plan to rejoin. The merge the launch will ask for is
        recorded as plan.json's `merge: {value, why}`: no for --no-merge (the keel), the blueprint's
        `merge: no`, or an unattended layer; else yes. A new ship's lease is written beside it,
        plans/<id>/skipper.json at `holder: yard, gen 0` (helm's bin/leaselib.py, S4): the yard holds
        it until the scope's skipper takes it. A lay into a plan that has a lease is fenced by it:
        --gen N (else SKIPPER_GEN, which a caller elsewhere sends as --gen) at another generation is
        refused, exit 4; with neither, the yard's side over ssh is a plain shell and passes, and a
        session on the yard itself passes only if it holds the lease.
    wharf apply --watch <blueprint.md>... [--plan ID] [--every MIN] [--launch] [--launches N]
        The skipper's one command per ship (yard-smooth, 2026-10-19): an apply every MIN minutes
        (default 5), each a fresh `bin/wharf apply` process, until every ship named has ended or the
        process is stopped. --launch: a `launch: finish` block whose predecessor ended is launched by
        `bin/autofinish-run <wt> --session <this session>` once the worktree's lock is free or
        handed over, at most N launches at once in its repo (default 2, from the worktrees'
        autofinish.json) and never past dispatch's run cap; its PR merged, it is reported `launched`;
        a launch that stopped is reported `waiting` with its gate, once; one the run cap refused
        is started again once a run ends. Attended only: refused under CLAUDE_UNATTENDED, the tick
        stays disarmed (D5-A).

What a pass does besides the diff's rows (yard-smooth): a block it ends — Orca completed it, or its
worker reported failed and its done_when holds all the same — has its worktree lock marked handed
over and its worker stopped (`worker-stop`); a block Orca put back to ready is not started again
when its done_when holds; each question a ship's worker asked the coordinator is relayed once to
the skipper (the file queue its next prompt prints, else the plan's `waiting` report). A
`skipper: scope` ship's question is hailed instead (S6) to the scope's skipper while it holds the
lease (helm's skipper, S5): `hail <its session> --kind ask --when idle --no-file` with HAIL_SPACE its
Talk page, a pointer naming the plan, the block and the question id (the question's text stays in
Orca: the pointer says how to read it), under hail's 400 characters. Never the file road, which a
scope skipper never reads: a hail no road took, or a ship no live skipper holds, is carded on the
board.
Work already on main is never built again (skipper-resilience S9): before a worker block starts, and
before an S1 retry of one, after one `git fetch origin <main>` per pass, `Ship.on_main` reads, cheapest
first: (1) done_when's `file` or `marker` on origin/<main>; (2) a merged PR whose head is the block's
branch (GitHub, PLAN_NO_GH skips it); (3) every file the block's branch changed identical on origin/<main>
(branches.prove, as `bin/pr` proves a carried branch); a hit ends the block `launched via <sha>` or
`launched via #N`. (4), before the first start only: an owned path (`owns:`, else the files its
predecessors' branches changed) moved on origin/<main> since the plan was made by a commit of no block of
this ship raises `a sibling may have built this (<sha>)` to the skipper, a `waiting` report; any later
report of the block (`helm report --status planned`) clears it, `--status launched` closes it. A fetch or
API failure is no hit, with one line on stderr: the reads only prevent duplicate work.
A `launch: finish` block whose predecessors were ended that way is ended too (launch_on_main).
    wharf status [<blueprint.md> | <ship>] [--plan ID] [--json]
        Where each block stands: the plan's status, Orca's Task, its newest Dispatch. Reads only.
    wharf status --orphans [--json]
        The Orca repos and Runs no plan on this Mac accounts for (a scratch ship's leftovers; Orca can
        remove neither). Reads only.
    wharf next <branch> [--repo DIR] [--json]
        `dispatch --next`'s question (wharf-on-orca S5, B9): is the caller a block of a ship with a
        block after it? The caller's own record decides: DISPATCH_SHIP (or the older DISPATCH_PLAN)
        and DISPATCH_TASK, the ship and
        block id wharf starts a session with, the block found in a blueprint that plan recorded (and
        in --repo's, when given); never a match of branch names across plans. Exit 0 and the next
        block(s) when one follows; exit 1, printing nothing, when the caller is no ship's block, is
        wharf's own start (a ship id without a block), or nothing follows it; exit 2 and a line on
        stderr when the check itself failed. Reads only; Orca is not asked: the graph is the file's,
        and `--next` must work with the Orca app shut.

The yard's fence (skipper-resilience S2): a ship whose repo's scope has a yard (`scopes set --yard`)
has one driver, the yard. A plain `wharf apply` of it (--watch too, whose passes are plain applies) is
refused off the yard, naming --yard, and on the yard too, where --yard lays and the tick drives; a dry
run, which writes nothing, is not. A scope with no yard (absent or null) applies as before.

Exit: 0 done; 1 refused (the file changed since its digest was accepted); 2 not a valid blueprint,
or refused by rule; 3 Orca not reachable; 4 another apply holds this ship's lock, or the ship's
lease refuses the caller's generation (--yard, S4).

What Orca provides is used, not rebuilt (the owner's D3-A rider, 2026-10-17; each probed by `--help`
on Orca 1.4.227): the Run (`run-create`, `run-use` when the coordinator died, `run-list` to find a
Run whose creation's answer was lost), the Tasks and their deps (`task-create --deps`, Orca makes a
Task `ready` when its deps complete — P3), the gates (`gate-create`, `gate-resolve`), the start
(`worker-start --task`, through the orca adapter's start(), the one bin/harness run uses), the
coordinator (`terminal create --worktree path:<repo>`: a Run's mutations need a terminal handle to
come `--from`, and a script has none of its own — P2, P6). Orca refuses a caller-chosen
`--retry-request` (P3), so a crash between a call and its record is recovered from Orca's own
state: a Task is found again by its title (the diff's `record` row), a Dispatch by `worker-list`,
a Run by its objective in `run-list`. What stays ours, because Orca has no slot for it: the
blueprint and its digest, the plan's ids and ledger, `done_when`, the memo answers behind a gate,
the gates on a start (`physical: none`, the week, depth 0, attended only), the worktree (made our
way and handed by `path:`, B6a's pick A), and the launch — Orca never launches.

Words: `skipper:` is read beside `manager:`; `launch:` is the release verb. Helm's words since rename
S5 (helm-vocabulary H1): its events are `helm report`'s, a block it reports merged is `launched` (`landed`
and `launched` both read as ended), a task names its block and its doer `by`, a seeded session gets
DISPATCH_SHIP beside DISPATCH_PLAN, and the ship's `started` is set by its first live apply. The store
keeps its names (plans/<id>/plan.json). An Orca block on another host (`host:` one of
the repo's hosts in repos.json) starts there: its house worktree made over ssh in the host's clone,
then `worker-start --on <host> --worktree path:<it>` (wharf-on-orca S3); refused while no Orca
environment is paired under the host's name. A claude-code block there starts by `dispatch --on`. Python 3.9, PyYAML (blueprintlib's), nothing of Claude's imported; no model call.
"""
import argparse
import fcntl
import json
import math
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import types
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
from pathlib import Path

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))
sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE.parent / "lib"))
import core_path  # noqa: E402 — the regatta core (C2); none: one line, exit 2
core_path.require()
import common  # noqa: E402
import blueprintlib  # noqa: E402
# helmlib (ships, their locks and events) and asklib are helm's (M11), still the overlay's until
# B12: found through the core, after this folder; without them there is no ship to check or apply.
# Exit 1, which dispatch's --next reads from `wharf next` as "not a ship's block": true where helm is
# absent, since every ship is helm's.
_HELMLIB = common.tool("helmlib.py")
if not _HELMLIB:
    sys.exit("wharf: helm's helmlib.py not found — wharf check and apply run on helm's ships")
sys.path.insert(2, str(_HELMLIB.parent))
import helmlib  # noqa: E402
# the ship's lease (skipper-resilience S4) is helm's too, beside helmlib; only --yard reads or writes
# it, so a helm without it — or one that will not load mid-edit — costs --yard alone (yard_lease),
# never a plain apply or the tick, which loads this file every pass
try:
    import leaselib  # noqa: E402
except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001
    leaselib = None

ENDED = ("done", "landed", "launched")   # `launched` is rename S2's word for `landed`: read both
PASSES = 10          # an apply's passes at most; a pass that acts on nothing ends it sooner
SHELL_TIMEOUT = 300  # a shell block's own timeout_seconds wins; over ~500 s it starts only from an attended apply (the tick has 600 s)
SESSION_START = 400  # what a session start may take: worker-start's 300 s and its 90 s wait, or pickup seed
TICK_STARTS = 2      # session starts per tick, every ship together: no run cap counts them yet (bin/harness)
HAIL_TEXT_MAX = 400  # bin/hail's TEXT_MAX: a hail's text is a pointer, and hail refuses a longer one
HAIL_TIMEOUT = 120   # one hail: its socket readback (HAIL_READBACK_S) and a Talk post, well inside the tick
HAIL_TAKEN = ("delivered", "queued", "held")   # what hail exits 0 for: a road took it (held: posted, unread yet)


def _mod(name, path):
    return SourceFileLoader(name, str(path)).load_module()


_cache = {}


def orca():
    if "orca" not in _cache:
        import importlib.util
        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("harness_adapter_orca", str(HERE / "harness_adapters" / "orca.py"))
        mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
        spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
        _cache["orca"] = mod
    return _cache["orca"]


def harness():
    """bin/harness as a module: its Ctx, Failed and guard()'s rules, so a start here is refused
    exactly where `harness run` refuses one."""
    if "harness" not in _cache:
        _cache["harness"] = _mod("harness_bin", HERE / "harness")
    return _cache["harness"]


def core():
    """hooks/common.py, the core's (read_owner, write_owner: the worktree lock's one writer)."""
    if "common" not in _cache:
        import common
        _cache["common"] = common
    return _cache["common"]


def read_json(path):
    try:
        d = json.loads(Path(path).read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return d if isinstance(d, dict) else None


def pid_alive(pid):
    try:
        os.kill(int(pid), 0)
        return True
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return False


def launch_live(state):
    """A launch whose `autofinish.json` in STATE (a worktree's `<git dir>/claude`) has not ended is
    under way while its waiter lives (`autofinish-waiter.json`'s pid), or for its first 10 minutes
    (bin/autofinish-run's PRE_START_S: the child may not have written the waiter yet). A runner
    that died without an end is not: autofinish-run's own refusals judge it at the next start."""
    st = read_json(Path(state) / "autofinish.json") or {}
    if pid_alive((read_json(Path(state) / "autofinish-waiter.json") or {}).get("pid")):
        return True
    try:
        import datetime
        return time.time() - datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(st.get("started") or "").timestamp() < 600
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return False


def worker_report(t):
    """The subject of an Orca Task's failed worker_done (its `result`, a JSON string Orca writes:
    provenance worker_report, outcome failed), or None: a Task failed any other way — a re-spec's
    `cancelled`, a failure set by hand — is no report."""
    r = t.get("result")
    if not isinstance(r, dict):   # a JSON string as Orca writes it; an object taken as read
        try:
            r = json.loads(r or "")
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            return None
    if not isinstance(r, dict) or r.get("provenance") != "worker_report" or str(r.get("outcome")).lower() != "failed":
        return None
    return " ".join(str(r.get("subject") or str(r.get("body") or "").split("\n")[0] or "no subject").split())[:160]


def say(*a):
    print(*a, flush=True)


def time_left():
    """Seconds until the caller's kill time (STALLS_DEADLINE: `ask poll` SIGKILLs the whole tick
    then), or None when there is none. Nothing is started that cannot finish before it."""
    try:
        d = float(os.environ.get("STALLS_DEADLINE") or 0)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return (d - time.time()) if d else None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- the plan and the file

def plan_id(given=None):
    pid = given or helmlib.env("ship") or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID")
    if not pid:
        raise SystemExit("wharf: no ship id — pass --plan, or run inside a session (DISPATCH_SHIP or DISPATCH_PLAN, "
                         "CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID)")
    return pid


def need(pid):
    p = helmlib.load_plan(pid)
    if p is None:
        raise SystemExit("wharf: no ship %s in %s (helm ship <topic>)" % (pid, helmlib.plans_root()))
    return p


def recorded(pid, path):
    """(key, accepted) a load of PATH in plan PID reads with (blueprintlib.load): the pin's repo of the
    record whose file PATH is (a pinned ship's copy), and every digest the plan has accepted."""
    recs = [r for r in ((helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}).get("blueprints") or {}).values() if isinstance(r, dict)]
    real = os.path.realpath(str(path))
    pin = next((r["pin"] for r in recs if isinstance(r.get("pin"), dict) and r.get("file")
                and os.path.realpath(r["file"]) == real), None)
    return (pin or {}).get("repo"), set(r["digest"] for r in recs if r.get("digest"))


def load_recorded(pid, path):
    """blueprintlib.load of PATH as plan PID records it (recorded()); raises as load does."""
    key, accepted = recorded(pid, path)
    return blueprintlib.load(path, key=key, accepted=accepted)


def load_blueprint(path, pid=None):
    """The blueprint at PATH, or exit 2 naming every problem. With PID, read as that plan records it:
    a pinned copy keyed on its pin's repo, and a ship in flight warned of a `host:` the yard rule
    would refuse a new compile (its yard_warnings)."""
    key, accepted = recorded(pid, path) if pid else (None, ())
    try:
        return blueprintlib.load(path, key=key, accepted=accepted)
    except blueprintlib.BlueprintError as e:
        print("wharf: %s is not a valid blueprint:" % path, file=sys.stderr)
        for x in e.problems:
            print("  - %s" % x, file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    except OSError as e:
        print("wharf: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)


def repo_dir(bp):
    """The blueprint's repo on this Mac: an absolute path as is, else a name under ~/projects."""
    return repo_path(bp["meta"]["repo"])


def repo_path(r):
    """A registry key's checkout under the core's projects folder (common.PROJECTS, the root
    blueprintlib.repo_key reads keys from), or an absolute path as is."""
    return Path(r) if r.startswith("/") else Path(common.PROJECTS) / r


def ship_repo(bp, rec):
    """(key, checkout) of a ship's repo: a pinned ship's is its pin's — the yard never reads the
    blueprint's `repo:`, which may be a path on the caller's Mac — else the blueprint's."""
    pin = (rec or {}).get("pin")
    r = pin["repo"] if isinstance(pin, dict) and pin.get("repo") else bp["meta"]["repo"]
    return r, repo_path(r)


def skipper(bp, pid=None):
    m = bp["meta"]
    who = m.get("skipper") or m.get("manager")
    if who != "scope":
        return who
    # `skipper: scope` (a blueprint `helm send` sent) names the scope's lease holder, never the sender:
    # plans/<pid>/skipper.json says who holds it (S4) — a skipper's session while its lease runs; the
    # yard's hold, a lapsed lease or none names no session, and a relay goes to the board
    if not (pid and leaselib):
        return None
    try:
        rec = leaselib.read(pid)
    except leaselib.Unreadable:
        return None
    if not rec or rec["holder"] == leaselib.YARD or leaselib.lapsed(pid, rec=rec):
        return None
    return rec.get("session")


def doc_path(bp, rel, rec=None):
    """A decision's doc: beside the blueprint's own checkout first (it lives on the blueprint's branch),
    then the repo's main checkout (a pinned ship's: its pin's)."""
    roots = []
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(Path(bp["path"]).resolve().parent), "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
        if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip():
            roots.append(Path(r.stdout.strip()))
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        pass
    roots.append(ship_repo(bp, rec)[1])
    for root in roots:
        if (root / rel).is_file():
            return root / rel
    return None


def pinned_doc(rec, rel):
    """A pinned ship's decision doc as its branch has it on origin, or None: the pin's text is the
    plan's copy, in no checkout, and the answers are commits on the branch (keel pull), so neither
    of doc_path's places has them until the branch merges. Fetched at most once a pass (Ship.apply
    clears the mark); a fetch that fails reads the origin ref as it last came."""
    pin, main = rec.get("pin"), rec.get("main")
    if not (isinstance(pin, dict) and pin.get("branch") and main and Path(main, ".git").exists()):
        return None
    done = _cache.setdefault("fetched", set())
    if (main, pin["branch"]) not in done:
        done.add((main, pin["branch"]))
        try:
            subprocess.run(["git", "-C", main, "fetch", "-q", "origin", pin["branch"]], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            pass
    return _git_text(main, "show", "origin/%s:%s" % (pin["branch"], rel))


def memo_answered(bp, rec=None, mode=None):
    """doc, items → (every item answered?, "D2 B; D3 A") by bin/keel's own reader. No network, but for
    a pinned ship (REC with a pin), whose doc is read from its branch on origin first (pinned_doc).

    In mode dnd or yolo (skipper-modes S3) a gate whose open items keel yolo would all take — under
    dnd none held (keel's dnd_held), under yolo every one with a bare pick — resolves as taken, with
    "taken unattended (dnd)" in its text: nothing is written to the doc here (it may sit in another
    session's worktree), and the block after it, a run in the same mode, writes the picks itself
    through its prompt's `keel yolo` gate. One item held, and the gate waits on the owner as before. dnd
    reads the contract's `physical:` in the doc's checkout — a pinned doc's in the ship's main —
    and with no checkout to read it in holds the item (keel's dnd_held reads None as physical)."""
    memo = _mod("memo", common.tool("keel") or HERE / "keel")

    def takeable(it, lines, physical):
        if mode == "dnd":
            return memo.dnd_held(it, lines, physical) is None
        rec = " ".join((it.get("recommended") or "").split())
        return bool(rec) and not memo.CONDITIONAL_RE.search(rec) and not memo.reopened(it, lines)

    def answered(rel, items):
        # the pinned branch's copy first; when it does not settle every item, doc_path's places too:
        # a doc answered on main (or a keel branch merged there) must not be hidden by a stale branch copy
        pinned = pinned_doc(rec, rel) if rec else None
        if pinned is not None:
            got = settle(pinned, rel, items, Path(rec["main"], rel) if rec.get("main") else None)
            if got[0]:
                return got
        p = doc_path(bp, rel, rec)
        if p is None:
            return got if pinned is not None else (False, "%s not found" % rel)
        return settle(p.read_text(), rel, items, p)

    def settle(text, rel, items, path):
        lines, found, _ = memo.parse(text)
        got = {it["id"]: it for it in found}
        missing = [i for i in items if i not in got]
        if missing:
            return False, "no %s in %s" % (", ".join(missing), rel)
        # yolo_settled, not answered: a session's own `> Proceeding with B` must not open a gate
        ok = all(memo.yolo_settled(got[i], lines) for i in items)
        if not ok and mode in ("dnd", "yolo"):
            # keel's doc_physical reads the checkout from the doc's folder, and a pinned doc new on its
            # branch has no folder in the ship's main: there, the nearest folder that is (the pinned
            # dnd case, skipper-modes follow-ups — it read None, so dnd held every such doc)
            at = path
            while at and not at.parent.is_dir() and at.parent != at.parent.parent:
                at = at.parent
            physical = memo.doc_physical(at) if mode == "dnd" and at else None
            open_ = [i for i in items if not memo.yolo_settled(got[i], lines)]
            if all(takeable(got[i], lines, physical) for i in open_):
                return True, "taken unattended (%s): %s" % (mode, "; ".join(
                    "%s %s" % (i, " ".join((got[i].get("recommended") or "").split())[:40]) for i in open_))
        return ok, "; ".join("%s %s" % (i, (got[i].get("answer") or "").strip().splitlines()[0][:40] if (got[i].get("answer") or "").strip() else "replied")
                             for i in items) if ok else None
    return answered


def ship_mode(pid, bp):
    """The ship's mode now (skipper-modes S1): plan.json, then the blueprint's `mode:` (a dry run before
    the first apply wrote it), the repo's scope, `default` — helmlib.task_mode."""
    return helmlib.task_mode(pid, None, str(repo_dir(bp)), bp_mode(pid, bp))[0]


def bp_mode(pid, bp):
    """The blueprint's `mode:` as this caller may record it (skipper-modes S3b): None when it would raise
    the ship's mode and the caller is unattended — a blueprint is a file any run can write, and a raise
    is a yes to merge. The refusal's words, for the apply's line, from bp_mode_refusal. None too once an
    apply refused it (plan.json's `mode_refused`): a refusal stands until the owner runs `helm mode` on the
    ship, which drops it; an attended apply says it again meanwhile."""
    if (helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}).get("mode_refused"):
        return None
    return None if bp_mode_refusal(pid, bp) else bp["meta"].get("mode")


def bp_ship_mode(pid, bp):
    """The ship's mode now, task_mode's (mode, where) pair — read once per judgement."""
    return helmlib.task_mode(pid, None, str(repo_dir(bp)))


def bp_mode_refusal(pid, bp, once=False, read=None):
    """The refusal's words when recording the blueprint's `mode:` would raise the ship's mode for this
    caller, else None. `once` (the helm tick's `wharf apply --once --all`, from launchd with no
    CLAUDE_UNATTENDED) counts as unattended: no person runs it (landing review 9). `read`: the ship's
    mode as bp_ship_mode read it, else read here."""
    m = bp["meta"].get("mode")
    env = dict(os.environ, CLAUDE_UNATTENDED=os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED") or "wharf apply --once") if once else None
    return m and helmlib.raise_refusal((read or bp_ship_mode(pid, bp))[0], m, env)


def bp_mode_torn(pid, bp, read=None):
    """True when the ship's mode reads `ask` only because repos.json is torn (helmlib.torn_read): a
    refusal judged against that ask is this apply's alone, never kept in `mode_refused`, so the next
    apply judges the blueprint's mode again once the registry reads (the follow-ups' landing review)."""
    torn_read = getattr(helmlib, "torn_read", None)
    return bool(torn_read and torn_read(read or bp_ship_mode(pid, bp)))


def bp_mode_judge(pid, bp, once=False):
    """(refusal or None, torn) from one read of the ship's mode: two reads let a registry that healed
    between them keep, in `mode_refused`, a refusal judged against the torn `ask` (the second landing
    review)."""
    read = bp_ship_mode(pid, bp)
    return bp_mode_refusal(pid, bp, once, read), bp_mode_torn(pid, bp, read)


def change_text(rec, d, sd):
    if rec.get("digest") == d:
        return "the digest accepted %s matches" % helmlib.iso(rec.get("accepted"))[:16]
    added, changed, removed = blueprintlib.changes(rec.get("blocks"), sd)
    parts = [("%s %s" % (w, ", ".join(x))) for w, x in (("added", added), ("changed", changed), ("removed", removed)) if x]
    return "changed since accepted %s: %s" % (helmlib.iso(rec.get("accepted"))[:16], "; ".join(parts) or "the front matter or the preamble")


def report(pid, task, status=None, progress=None, **extra):
    """A `helm report` line, written as bin/helm's report writes it (one O_APPEND line)."""
    ev = {"task": task, "session": None, "host": helmlib.host(), "harness": "wharf", "plan": pid}
    for k, v in (("status", status), ("progress", progress)):
        if v:
            ev[k] = v
    ev.update({k: v for k, v in extra.items() if v is not None})
    try:
        helmlib.append_event(pid, ev)
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print("wharf: report %s skipped (%s)" % (task, e), file=sys.stderr)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- Orca's reads

def orca_reads(run, coordinator=None):
    """({"run", "tasks", "gates", "workers"}, None) or (None, why): the four reads of Q2, through the
    orca adapter's one CLI path (HARNESS_ORCA, ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE cleared). Reads only."""
    o = orca()
    if not o._app_up():
        return None, "Orca is not running here (the app's runtime answers the CLI)"
    out = {}
    res, err = o._call(None, ["orchestration", "run-show", "--id", run])
    if err:
        return None, err
    out["run"] = (res or {}).get("run") or res
    coord = coordinator or (out["run"] or {}).get("coordinator_handle")
    res, err = o._call(None, ["orchestration", "task-list", "--run", run] + (["--from", coord] if coord else []))
    if err:
        return None, err
    out["tasks"] = (res or {}).get("tasks") or []
    res, err = o._call(None, ["orchestration", "gate-list", "--run", run])
    if err:
        return None, err
    out["gates"] = (res or {}).get("gates") or []
    rows, cursor = [], None
    for _ in range(20):
        res, err = o._call(None, ["orchestration", "worker-list", "--run", run, "--limit", "100", "--include-remote"] + (["--cursor", cursor] if cursor else []))
        if err:
            return None, err
        rows += (res or {}).get("workers") or []
        page = (res or {}).get("page") or {}
        cursor = page.get("nextCursor")
        if not (page.get("hasMore") and cursor):
            break
    out["workers"] = rows
    return out, None


def plan_status(pid):
    try:
        return {t["id"]: t for t in helmlib.state(pid)["tasks"]}
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — a state that will not merge reads as no reports yet
        return {}


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- check (B6's `plan chain`)

def cmd_check(a):
    bp = load_blueprint(a.file, a.plan)
    here = helmlib.host()
    d, sd = blueprintlib.digest(bp), blueprintlib.block_digests(bp)
    if a.json and a.accept:
        raise SystemExit("wharf check: --json prints the graph only; --accept separately")
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(blueprintlib.as_json(bp, here), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True))
        return 0
    for line in blueprintlib.graph_lines(bp, here):
        say(line)
    if not (a.accept or a.plan):
        return 0
    pid = plan_id(a.plan)
    p = need(pid)
    rec = (p.get("blueprints") or {}).get(bp["name"])
    if not a.accept:
        say("plan %s: %s" % (pid, change_text(rec, d, sd) if rec and rec.get("digest")
                             else "no digest of %s recorded (wharf check --accept)" % bp["name"]))
        return 0
    held = lock(pid, bp["name"])
    if held is None:
        say("wharf check --accept: %s is being applied right now (its lock in %s): accept once it ends" % (bp["name"], helmlib.plan_dir(pid)))
        return 4
    try:
        with helmlib.locked(pid):
            p = need(pid)
            rec = dict((p.get("blueprints") or {}).get(bp["name"]) or {})
            if rec.get("pin") and rec.get("file") and os.path.realpath(a.file) != os.path.realpath(rec["file"]):
                # accept() would point a pinned ship at this file, out of its pin (apply_ship's guard)
                say("wharf check --accept: %s refused — it is pinned (%s): its blueprint is %s, and "
                    "`wharf apply --yard` rejoins it" % (bp["name"], pin_label(rec["pin"]), rec["file"]))
                return 2
            before = change_text(rec, d, sd) if rec.get("digest") else None
            accept(rec, a.file, d, sd)
            p.setdefault("blueprints", {})[bp["name"]] = rec
            helmlib.save_plan(p)
    finally:
        held.close()
    say("accepted %s into plan %s: digest %s%s" % (bp["name"], pid, d[:12], (" (was: %s)" % before) if before else ""))
    return 0


def accept(rec, path, d, sd):
    f = Path(path).resolve()
    rec.update(file=str(f), digest=d, blocks=sd, accepted=helmlib.now(), by=os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID"))
    pin = rec.get("pin")
    if pin:
        # a pinned ship (wharf apply --yard): its file is the plan's copy, in no checkout; where it sits
        # in its repo is the pin's, so blueprint_file() and doc_path() find the repo with no branch here
        rec.update(main=str(repo_path(pin["repo"])), rel=pin["rel"], by=rec["by"] or (rec.get("laid_by") or {}).get("session"))
        return
    # where it sits in its repo: a file accepted from a worktree is found on the main checkout once
    # the worktree is gone (its branch launched), as doc_path does
    gd = _git(f.parent, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir")
    prefix = _git(f.parent, "rev-parse", "--show-prefix")   # git's own spelling: no relative_to on a case-insensitive disk
    if gd and prefix is not None:
        rec.update(main=str(Path(gd).parent), rel=prefix + f.name)


def blueprint_file(rec):
    """The recorded blueprint, else the same path on the repo's main checkout, else None."""
    if rec.get("file") and Path(rec["file"]).is_file():
        return rec["file"]
    if rec.get("main") and rec.get("rel"):
        alt = Path(rec["main"]) / rec["rel"]
        if alt.is_file():
            return str(alt)
    return None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- apply: the gates on a start

def paired(name):
    """True when Orca on this Mac holds a saved environment named NAME (`orca environment list`),
    False when it holds none so named, None when Orca can't be asked. The S3 recipe pairs a host
    under its repos.json name: `orca environment add --name <host> --pairing-code <link>`."""
    o = orca()
    res, err = o._call(None, ["environment", "list"])
    if err:
        return None
    return any(isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("name") == name for e in (res or {}).get("environments") or [])


def remote_refusal(s):
    """Why a block on another host does not start, or None: an Orca block starts once Orca here holds
    an environment paired under the host's name (Ship.start_orca: a house worktree there over ssh, then
    `worker-start --on <host> --worktree path:<it>`, the start S3 proved on 2026-10-18)."""
    h = s["host"]
    doc = "docs/wharf-on-orca-2026-10-17.md S3"
    if s.get("provider") == "claude-code":
        return "host: %s — a claude-code block there starts by `dispatch --on %s`, not from apply yet (%s)" % (h, h, doc)
    ok = paired(h)
    if ok is None:
        return "host: %s — Orca could not list its environments (orca environment list)" % h
    if not ok:
        return "host: %s — no Orca environment paired as %s (orca environment list; %s pairs one)" % (h, h, doc)
    return None


def start_refusal(bp, st, repo):
    """Why this block may not start now, or None. A session start (orca, claude-code) is attended
    and at depth 0 only (bin/harness's guard; the 10-15 doc's Q2: a ship is flat), on a repo whose
    contract says `physical: none`, with a login whose week is not tight (bin/autofinish's
    week_tight: `account pick --cached`). A shell block passes the first two: it starts no session."""
    s = st["raw"]
    if blueprintlib.remote_host(s, helmlib.host()):
        why = remote_refusal(s)
        if why:
            return why
    if s.get("physical") and s["physical"] != "none":
        return "physical: %s — apply starts only physical: none" % s["physical"]
    why = harness().physical_ok(str(repo))
    if why:
        return why
    if s.get("provider") == "shell":
        return None
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"):
        return "a session start is attended only (CLAUDE_UNATTENDED=%s): the tick starts it from launchd" % os.environ["CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"]
    depth = os.environ.get("DISPATCH_DEPTH") or "0"
    if depth not in ("", "0"):
        return "a ship starts its blocks at depth 0 (DISPATCH_DEPTH=%s)" % depth
    if s.get("provider") == "orca" and s.get("agent") == "codex" and harness().public_repo(str(repo)):
        return "Codex does not run in %s: a public repo (contract E4)" % repo
    if not os.environ.get("WHARF_NO_WEEK"):
        try:
            af = _cache.get("autofinish") or _mod("autofinish_bin", HERE / "autofinish")
            _cache["autofinish"] = af
            verdict, detail = af.week_tight(str(repo))
        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
            verdict, detail = "none", "the week could not be read (%s)" % type(e).__name__
        if verdict:
            return "the week says %s: %s" % (verdict, detail)
    return None


# Ship.worktree()'s recipe on another host, read by `sh -s -- <repo under ~/projects> <topic> <branch>
# <plan/ship>` over ssh; prints the worktree's absolute path last. Exit 2 no clone, 3 not from local
# main, 4 on another branch, 5 another ship's (the same refusals as here).
REMOTE_WORKTREE = r'''set -u
rel=$1 topic=$2 br=$3 mine=$4
cd "$HOME/projects/$rel" 2>/dev/null || { echo "no clone at ~/projects/$rel" >&2; exit 2; }
p="$PWD/.claude/worktrees/$topic"
if [ -d "$p" ]; then
  [ "$(git -C "$p" symbolic-ref --short -q HEAD)" = "$br" ] || { echo "$p is not on $br" >&2; exit 4; }
  own="$(git -C "$p" rev-parse --absolute-git-dir)/wharf-ship"
  if [ -f "$own" ]; then
    [ "$(cat "$own")" = "$mine" ] || { echo "$p is ship $(cat "$own")'s worktree, not $mine's" >&2; exit 5; }
  elif ! git -C "$p" merge-base --is-ancestor main HEAD; then
    echo "$br does not fork from local main" >&2; exit 3
  fi
  echo "$p"; exit 0
fi
# the host's main moves only when a session starts there (sync.py): bring a clean one up to origin
# first, as sync.py would. Every command reads /dev/null: the recipe itself is sh's stdin (review 2026-10-18)
if [ "$(git symbolic-ref --short -q HEAD)" = main ] && [ -z "$(git status --porcelain </dev/null)" ]; then
  git fetch -q origin main </dev/null && git merge --ff-only -q origin/main </dev/null || echo "main not brought up to origin; forking from local main" >&2
fi
if git show-ref --verify --quiet "refs/heads/$br"; then git worktree add -q "$p" "$br" </dev/null; else git worktree add -q "$p" -b "$br" main </dev/null; fi || exit 1
if [ -e .env ] && [ ! -e "$p/.env" ]; then ln -s "$PWD/.env" "$p/.env"; fi
git -C "$p" merge-base --is-ancestor main HEAD || { echo "$br does not fork from local main" >&2; exit 3; }
printf '%s\n' "$mine" > "$(git -C "$p" rev-parse --absolute-git-dir)/wharf-ship"
echo "$p"
'''


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- apply: one ship

def marker_built(lines, anchor):
    """Whether a done_when marker holds in the doc's lines: its anchor's item says "built" (the one reader,
    for the worktree's file and for a blob on origin/main alike)."""
    # the convention (iac section 6): the block wrote "Built" under its item — the item's own
    # lines only (up to the next item or heading), and the word, never "not built" or "rebuilt"
    item = re.compile(r"(^#|^\s*(?:[-*]|\d+\.)\s|^\s*\*\*|^\s*\|)")
    built = re.compile(r"(?<![\w-])built(?![\w-])", re.I)   # never "built-ins"
    unbuilt = re.compile(r"\b(?:not(?:\s+yet)?|never|un)\s*-?\s*built\b|\bbuilt\s*\?|\bonce\b[^.]*\bbuilt\b|\bis\s+built\s+(?:before|first)\b", re.I)
    # the anchor's own item: a heading, list item, bold lead or table row that starts with
    # the anchor (after its marker), never a line that merely mentions it ("starts S3 once S1 is built")
    # also an item line that names it bold anywhere ("1. **Built 2026-10-16** — … **B6a — x**":
    # this repo rewrites a step's line when it is built)
    e = re.escape(anchor)
    lead = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:#+|[-*]|\d+\.|\|)?\s*(?:\*\*|`)?%s(?![\w-])|^\s*(?:#+|[-*]|\d+\.|\|)\s.*?\*\*%s(?![\w-])" % (e, e))
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        if not lead.match(line):
            continue
        for j, x in enumerate(lines[i:i + 12]):
            if j and item.match(x) and not x.lstrip().startswith(">"):
                break
            if built.search(x) and not unbuilt.search(x):
                return True
    return False


class Ship:
    """One apply over one blueprint in one plan: the plan, its record of the ship, the ledger."""

    def __init__(self, pid, bp, dry, launch=None):
        self.pid, self.bp, self.dry = pid, bp, dry
        self.launch = launch   # {"launches": N, "session": id or None}: --launch starts `launch: finish` blocks
        self.p = need(pid)
        self.rec = (self.p.get("blueprints") or {}).get(bp["name"]) or {}
        self.repo_key, self.repo = ship_repo(bp, self.rec)
        self.here = helmlib.host()
        self.did = []   # what this apply did, one line each
        self.checks = {}   # done_when `check:` results, read once per apply

    def reload(self):
        """plan.json read again (after the ship's lock: what an earlier reader saw may be stale)."""
        self.p = need(self.pid)
        self.rec = (self.p.get("blueprints") or {}).get(self.bp["name"]) or {}

    def clash(self):
        """A block id that is already another ship's plan task: plan task ids are one namespace per
        plan, so a second ship's `build` would read the first one's ended `build` as its own."""
        mine = self.bp["name"]
        # a task with no ship is one made by hand (`helm task`) or by `helm compile`: its reports
        # would read as the block's own (a `done` there completes the block's Task unstarted)
        return ["%s (%s)" % (s["id"], ("ship %s" % t["ship"]) if t.get("ship") else "a plan task of no ship")
                for s in self.bp["blocks"] for t in [(self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(s["id"])]
                if t is not None and t.get("ship") != mine]

    def save(self):
        """Only this ship's part written: under the plan's lock, plan.json is read again and this
        ship's record and plan tasks replace theirs, so another writer's tasks, ships or space
        survive an apply that runs for minutes (bin/helm, the tick, a second ship). `started` is the
        ship's start (helm-vocabulary C5: the keel laid), set once by its first apply (apply_ship)."""
        if self.dry:
            return
        with helmlib.locked(self.pid):
            fresh = helmlib.load_plan(self.pid) or self.p
            if self.p.get("started") and not fresh.get("started"):
                fresh["started"] = self.p["started"]
            if self.p.get("mode") and "mode" not in fresh:   # the blueprint's, once; `helm mode` since wins
                fresh["mode"] = self.p["mode"]
            # a refusal this apply wrote (apply_ship), kept as `mode` is: without it the key never reached
            # plan.json and the next tick recorded the run-written mode (the follow-ups' landing review).
            # Only this apply's own: one `helm mode` cleared since, or a mode set since, stays as it is
            if getattr(self, "refused_now", None) and "mode" not in fresh and not fresh.get("mode_refused"):
                fresh["mode_refused"] = self.refused_now
            fresh.setdefault("blueprints", {})[self.bp["name"]] = self.rec
            ft = fresh.setdefault("tasks", {})
            for sid, t in (self.p.get("tasks") or {}).items():
                if sid in self.bp["by_id"] or t.get("ship") == self.bp["name"]:
                    # the keys wharf writes (plan_fields' and its own), set or removed; the rest (an ETA, a
                    # `helm task --owns` on a block that declares no owns) is whoever wrote it since this apply read the plan
                    have, owned = ft.setdefault(sid, {}), self.owned_keys(sid)
                    for k in owned:
                        if k in t:
                            have[k] = t[k]
                        else:
                            have.pop(k, None)
                    for k in set(t) - owned:
                        have.setdefault(k, t[k])
            helmlib.save_plan(fresh)
            self.p = fresh

    WHARF_KEYS = {"orca_task", "orca_dispatches", "seeded_branch", "branch", "stopped", "wt_deferred", "sibling_seen", "on_main"}

    def owned_keys(self, sid):
        st = self.bp["by_id"].get(sid)
        if not st:
            return set(self.WHARF_KEYS)
        return set(blueprintlib.plan_fields(self.bp, st, self.here, self.repo_key)) | self.WHARF_KEYS

    def task(self, sid):
        return self.p.setdefault("tasks", {}).setdefault(sid, {})

    # -- the request ledger: one line before each call, completed after it --------------------

    def intent(self, op, block, **k):
        e = dict(op=op, block=block, at=helmlib.now(), state="sent", **k)
        self.rec.setdefault("ledger", []).append(e)
        self.save()
        crash = os.environ.get("WHARF_CRASH")   # tests: "<op>:<block>" dies after the call, before the record
        return e, crash == "%s:%s" % (op, block)

    def settle(self, e, crash, result=None, error=None):
        if crash:
            os._exit(9)
        e["state"] = "failed" if error else "done"
        if error:
            e["error"] = str(error)[:300]
        for k in ("id", "request"):
            if result and result.get(k):
                e[k] = result[k]
        self.save()

    def dangling(self):
        """Ledger lines sent and never settled: a crash between a call and its record. Each is
        marked once, and Orca's own state decides what follows (module docstring)."""
        out = [e for e in self.rec.get("ledger") or [] if e.get("state") == "sent"]
        for e in out:
            e["state"] = "unknown"
        if out:
            self.save()
        return out

    def call(self, op, block, args, timeout=120):
        """One Orca mutation through the adapter's CLI path, ledgered: (result, None) or (None, why)."""
        e, crash = self.intent(op, block)
        res, err = orca()._call(None, args, timeout=timeout)
        o = orca()
        self.settle(e, crash, {"id": o._first(res or {}, "task.id", "gate.id", "run.id", "dispatch.id", "id"),
                               "request": o._first(res or {}, "mutation.requestId", "requestId")}, err)
        return res, err

    # -- the Run and its coordinator ------------------------------------------------------------

    def objective(self):
        return "%s/%s (wharf apply, plan %s)" % (self.bp["meta"]["repo"], self.bp["name"], self.pid)

    def coordinator_alive(self, h):
        res, err = orca()._call(None, ["terminal", "show", "--terminal", h], timeout=30)
        if err and re.search(r"\((?:terminal|terminal_tab|session_tab)_not_found\)", str(err)):   # orca._call's "(<code>)"
            return False
        if err:   # a timeout or a busy runtime is not a dead coordinator: a new one would orphan it
            raise Refused("terminal show %s: %s" % (h, str(err)[:200]), 3)
        # a closed terminal still answers `terminal show` (1.4.227, live 2026-10-17): `connected:
        # false` and an `exitCause` ({"kind": "operator_close"}) say it is gone
        term = orca()._first(res or {}, "terminal") or {}
        return term.get("connected") is not False and not term.get("exitCause")

    def new_coordinator(self):
        """A shell in the repo's main checkout, the Run's home terminal (P2: a path selector works
        for any worktree Orca knows; the repo is registered — `orca repo add` once, below)."""
        try:
            orca()._repo_id(harness().Ctx(), str(self.repo))   # `repo add` when Orca does not know it: a live write, said
        except harness().Failed as e:
            raise Refused("Orca does not know %s and would not add it: %s" % (self.repo, e), 1)
        res, err = self.call("terminal-create", None, ["terminal", "create", "--worktree", "path:%s" % self.repo,
                                                       "--title", "wharf %s" % self.bp["name"]], timeout=60)
        h = orca()._first(res or {}, "terminal.handle", "handle")
        if err or not h:
            raise Refused("Orca opened no coordinator terminal in %s: %s" % (self.repo, err or json.dumps(res)[:200]), 1)
        return h

    def ensure_run(self):
        """(run id, coordinator): recorded ones, a dead coordinator replaced (`run-use`), a Run
        whose creation's answer was lost found by its objective (`run-list`), else run-create."""
        run, coord = self.rec.get("orca_run"), self.rec.get("coordinator")
        if run:
            if coord and self.coordinator_alive(coord):
                return run, coord
            coord = self.new_coordinator()
            _, err = self.call("run-use", None, ["orchestration", "run-use", "--id", run, "--from", coord])
            if err:
                orca()._call(None, ["terminal", "close", "--terminal", coord, "--tab"], timeout=60)   # no tab left per refused pass
                raise Refused("run-use %s from a new coordinator: %s" % (run, err), 1)
            self.rec["coordinator"] = coord
            self.save()
            self.did.append("coordinator %s took Run %s (the last one is gone)" % (coord, run))
            return run, coord
        # a failed run-create counts too: Orca's own CLI says an unknown-outcome error "may already
        # have taken effect", and our timeout reads as failed; the objective names this plan, so a hit is ours
        lost = [e for e in self.rec.get("ledger") or [] if e.get("op") == "run-create" and e.get("state") in ("unknown", "failed")]
        if lost:
            hit, cursor = [], None
            for _ in range(20):
                res, err = orca()._call(None, ["orchestration", "run-list", "--limit", "100"] + (["--cursor", cursor] if cursor else []))
                if err:
                    break
                hit += [r for r in (res or {}).get("runs") or [] if r.get("objective") == self.objective()]
                # Orca 1.4.230 answers `nextCursor` at the top level; the `page` object is read for older ones
                page = (res or {}).get("page") or {}
                cursor = (res or {}).get("nextCursor") or (page.get("nextCursor") if page.get("hasMore") else None)
                if hit or not cursor:
                    break
            if hit:
                self.rec.update(orca_run=hit[0].get("id"), coordinator=hit[0].get("coordinator_handle") or coord)
                self.save()
                self.did.append("Run %s found by its objective (its creation's answer was lost)" % self.rec["orca_run"])
                return self.ensure_run()
        coord = coord if coord and self.coordinator_alive(coord) else self.new_coordinator()
        self.rec["coordinator"] = coord
        self.save()
        res, err = self.call("run-create", None, ["orchestration", "run-create", "--objective", self.objective(), "--from", coord])
        run = orca()._first(res or {}, "run.id", "id", "runId")
        if err or not run:
            raise Refused("run-create: %s" % (err or json.dumps(res)[:200]), 1)
        self.rec.update(orca_run=run, coordinator=coord, created_run=helmlib.now())
        self.save()
        self.did.append("Run %s created, coordinator %s" % (run, coord))
        return run, coord

    # -- the worktree, our way ------------------------------------------------------------------

    def worktree(self, st):
        """(path, branch) of a block's worktree: `.claude/worktrees/<topic>` on its branch from local
        main (or the newer origin/<main> on_main fetched this pass), the .env linked (rules/git-workflow.md's recipe; B6a's pick A). Made once; a second
        apply finds it."""
        br = blueprintlib.branch_of(self.bp, st, self.here)
        topic = re.sub(r"^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-", "", br.rsplit("/", 1)[-1])
        path = self.repo / ".claude" / "worktrees" / topic
        mine = "%s/%s" % (self.pid, self.bp["name"])
        if path.is_dir():
            got = _git(path, "symbolic-ref", "--short", "-q", "HEAD")
            if got != br:
                raise Refused("%s is on %s, not %s" % (path, got, br), 2)
            gd = _git(path, "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir")
            owner = (Path(gd) / "wharf-ship") if gd else None
            had = owner.read_text().strip() if owner and owner.is_file() else None
            if had and had != mine:
                raise Refused("%s is ship %s's worktree, not %s's (a block id two ships share)" % (path, had, mine), 2)
            # R1 here too: a worktree an earlier apply left after refusing it is still refused
            if not had and subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(path), "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", "main", "HEAD"],
                                          capture_output=True).returncode:
                raise Refused("%s does not fork from local main" % br, 2)
            return path, br
        # a new branch starts from the origin/<main> this pass fetched (on_main) when local main is behind
        # it: a predecessor the on-main reads ended is on origin only. --no-track: never upstream onto main
        # (rules: a branch tracking origin/main is pushed onto it). R1 below still holds.
        base, fetched = "main", (_cache.get("onmain") or {}).get(str(self.repo))
        if fetched and _git(self.repo, "rev-parse", "main") != _git(self.repo, "rev-parse", fetched) and \
                not subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(self.repo), "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", "main", fetched],
                                   capture_output=True).returncode:
            base = fetched
        argv = ["worktree", "add", str(path), br] if _git(self.repo, "show-ref", "--verify", "--quiet", "refs/heads/" + br) is not None \
            else ["worktree", "add", "--no-track", "-b", br, str(path), base]
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(self.repo)] + argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            r = None
        if r is None or r.returncode:
            raise Refused("git worktree add %s: %s" % (path, (r.stderr or "").strip()[-200:] if r else "timed out"), 1)
        if (self.repo / ".env").exists() and not os.path.lexists(str(path / ".env")):
            os.symlink(str(self.repo / ".env"), str(path / ".env"))
        # R1: the tip is on local main (a reused branch must not carry another base)
        if subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(path), "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", "main", "HEAD"], capture_output=True).returncode:
            raise Refused("%s does not fork from local main" % br, 2)
        gd = _git(path, "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir")
        if gd:
            (Path(gd) / "wharf-ship").write_text(mine + "\n")   # whose it is: one ship per worktree
        return path, br

    def remote_worktree(self, st, host):
        """(path on HOST, branch) of an Orca block's worktree there: worktree()'s recipe and checks, run
        over ssh in the host's clone (~/projects/<this repo's path under ~/projects>), the path read
        back from the host for the exact `path:` selector — Orca refuses `current` and `new-child`
        remotely. The ssh alias is bin/harness's PEERS; WHARF_SSH stands in for ssh (tests)."""
        peer = harness().peers().get(host)   # PEERS plus HARNESS_PEER_<HOST>, never this machine
        if not peer:
            raise Refused("host %s has no ssh alias (bin/harness PEERS or HARNESS_PEER_%s)" % (host, host.upper()), 2)
        br = blueprintlib.branch_of(self.bp, st, self.here)
        topic = re.sub(r"^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-", "", br.rsplit("/", 1)[-1])
        try:
            rel = self.repo.resolve().relative_to((Path.home() / "projects").resolve())
        except ValueError:
            raise Refused("%s is not under ~/projects: no clone of it on %s to name" % (self.repo, host), 2)
        args = " ".join(shlex.quote(x) for x in (str(rel), topic, br, "%s/%s" % (self.pid, self.bp["name"])))
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([os.environ.get("WHARF_SSH") or "ssh", "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=10",
                                peer, "sh -s -- " + args], input=REMOTE_WORKTREE, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=90)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            raise Refused("the worktree on %s: %s" % (host, e), 1)
        lines = (r.stdout or "").strip().splitlines()
        if r.returncode or not lines or not lines[-1].startswith("/"):
            # 2 no clone, 3 not from local main, 4 another branch, 5 another ship's: the recipe's refusals
            raise Refused("the worktree on %s: %s" % (host, ((r.stderr or "").strip() or "exit %d" % r.returncode)[-200:]),
                          2 if r.returncode in (2, 3, 4, 5) else 1)
        return lines[-1], br

    def branch(self, st):
        """A block's branch: the one pickup seed made (read back), else the blueprint's."""
        return (self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(st["id"], {}).get("seeded_branch") or blueprintlib.branch_of(self.bp, st, self.here)

    def wt_of(self, sid):
        st = self.bp["by_id"].get(sid)
        br = self.branch(st) if st else None
        if not br or blueprintlib.remote_host(st["raw"], self.here):   # a remote block's worktree is on its host
            return None
        return self.repo / ".claude" / "worktrees" / re.sub(r"^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-", "", br.rsplit("/", 1)[-1])

    # -- the starts, one per provider -----------------------------------------------------------

    def started(self, sid, task=None):
        """The ledger line of a shell or claude-code block this ship already started, or None: Orca
        keeps its Task `ready`, so the ledger is the word (an Orca block's start is Orca's own Dispatch).
        A shell line counts for its own Task only: a re-specced block's new Task runs its command. A
        seed counts for the block (its branch exists whatever the Task); one cut off mid-call
        (`unknown`) counts only when its branch is there to prove it."""
        hit = []
        for e in self.rec.get("ledger") or []:
            if e.get("block") != sid or e.get("state") not in ("done", "unknown"):
                continue
            if e.get("op") == "shell" and (task is None or e.get("task") in (None, task)):
                hit.append(e)
            elif e.get("op") == "seed" and (e["state"] == "done" or self.seed_branch_found(sid, e)):
                hit.append(e)
        return hit[-1] if hit else None

    def seed_branch_found(self, sid, e):
        """An `unknown` seed's branch, read back (`claude/<host>/<date>-<sid>`): recorded on the line
        and the task when found, else the line is marked failed (nothing was made)."""
        if e.get("id"):
            return True
        refs = _git(self.repo, "for-each-ref", "--format=%(refname:short)", "refs/heads/claude/") or ""
        # pickup seed's own name: claude/<this host>/<a date from the line's day on>-<sid>
        day = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d", time.localtime(e.get("at") or 0))
        hits = [r for r in refs.splitlines() if re.match(r"claude/%s/(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})-%s$" % (re.escape(self.here), re.escape(sid)), r)
                and re.match(r"claude/[^/]+/(\S{10})", r).group(1) >= day]
        if not hits:
            if not self.dry:
                e["state"], e["error"] = "failed", "cut off before it said; no branch for %s" % sid
                self.save()
            return False
        if not self.dry:
            e["id"] = hits[-1]
            self.task(sid)["seeded_branch"] = self.task(sid)["branch"] = hits[-1]
            self.save()
        return True

    def spent(self, st):
        """Why a block's starts are used up, or None. Asked before the tick counts a start. A start
        that ran (a Dispatch made, a seed made) counts against the first and the block's retries
        (0–2); one that failed before anything ran counts against two more, so a passing hiccup is
        tried again and a start that always fails still stops. Per Orca Task for a worker: a
        re-specced block starts afresh."""
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        op = {"orca": "worker-start", "claude-code": "seed"}.get(s["provider"])
        if not op:
            return None
        cur = ((self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(sid) or {}).get("orca_task")
        mine = [e for e in self.rec.get("ledger") or [] if e.get("block") == sid and e.get("op") == op
                and (op == "seed" or e.get("task") in (None, cur))]
        ran = [e for e in mine if e.get("state") != "failed"]
        failed = [e for e in mine if e.get("state") == "failed"]
        allowed = 1 + int(s.get("retries") or 0)
        if len(ran) < allowed and len(failed) < allowed + 2:
            return None
        why = ("started %d times already" % len(ran)) if len(ran) >= allowed else ("%d starts failed before anything ran" % len(failed))
        if not self.dry and (plan_status(self.pid).get(sid) or {}).get("status") != "failed":
            report(self.pid, sid, "failed", "%s: %s (retries %d), not started again" % (op, why, allowed - 1))
        return "not started: %s (retries %d)" % (why, allowed - 1)

    def start(self, st, task, run, coord):
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        e = self.started(sid, task) if s["provider"] != "orca" else None
        if e and s["provider"] == "shell":
            # the command ran (or was cut off) and Orca still says `ready`: its end never reached the
            # Task — send it again from this pass's coordinator, never the command
            if self.dry:
                return "started already (the ledger): would send its end to Orca again"
            rc = e.get("id") if e.get("state") == "done" else None
            status = "completed" if rc == "0" else "failed"
            text = ("exit %s (sent again)" % rc) if rc is not None else "interrupted: the command's result was never recorded"
            _, err = self.call("task-update", sid, ["orchestration", "task-update", "--id", task, "--status", status,
                                                    "--result", text, "--run", run, "--from", coord])
            if err:
                return "started already (the ledger): its end not taken again — %s" % err
            return "sent its end again (the ledger: it ran once): %s" % status
        if e:
            return "started already (the ledger): its end completes the Task"
        built = self.built_before_retry(st, task)
        if built:
            return built
        onmain = self.on_main(st, task)
        if onmain:
            return onmain
        spent = self.spent(st)
        if spent:
            return spent
        why = start_refusal(self.bp, st, self.repo)
        if why:
            return "refused: %s" % why
        braked = None if blueprintlib.remote_host(s, self.here) else brake_refusal()
        if braked:
            # constant text: a standing refusal is said once (say_once), classed `refuse` and never
            # escalated (the brake is the owner's own, on purpose). A block on another host is not
            # held: the brake read here is this Mac's, and the other Mac's is not read yet
            return "braked: a start waits for the studio brake"
        need_s = (int(s.get("timeout_seconds") or SHELL_TIMEOUT) if s["provider"] == "shell" else SESSION_START)
        if blueprintlib.remote_host(s, self.here):
            need_s += 90   # remote_worktree's ssh, before the start
        left = time_left()
        if left is not None and left < need_s + 30:
            # no count of seconds left in the line: it changes every tick, and the tick says a
            # standing refusal once (.said)
            return "refused: it needs %ds, more than is left before the tick's kill time (the next attended apply or tick)" % need_s
        if s["provider"] != "shell" and _cache.get("tick") is not None:
            if _cache["tick"] >= TICK_STARTS:
                return "refused: %d session starts this tick already (TICK_STARTS)" % TICK_STARTS
        if s["provider"] == "shell" and s.get("launch") == "finish":
            return self.start_shell(st, task, run, coord)   # it runs no command: a launch, or the skipper's (dry inside)
        if self.dry:
            return "would start (%s)" % s["provider"]
        if s["provider"] != "shell" and _cache.get("tick") is not None:
            _cache["tick"] += 1
        if s["provider"] == "shell":
            return self.start_shell(st, task, run, coord)
        if s["provider"] == "orca":
            return self.start_orca(st, task, run, coord)
        return self.start_claude_code(st, task, run, coord)

    def worktree_known(self, st, path):
        """False once, when Orca's own registry does not list the worktree git just made: the first
        S1 probe (2026-10-21) got `selector_not_found` seconds after `git worktree add`, and a start
        that fails before anything ran counts against the block (spent()). Orca owns that registry
        (no `worktree add` of ours), so the start waits one pass; a second pass that still finds it
        absent starts anyway, and a real failure then counts as it always did. A list that cannot be
        read, or is cut off before the path, never holds a start back."""
        t = self.task(st["id"])
        res, err = orca()._call(None, ["worktree", "list", "--repo", "path:%s" % self.repo, "--limit", "1000"], timeout=60)
        rows = (res or {}).get("worktrees")
        if err or not isinstance(rows, list) or (res or {}).get("truncated"):
            return True
        want = os.path.realpath(str(path))
        if any(os.path.realpath(str(r.get("path") or "")) == want for r in rows if isinstance(r, dict)):
            if t.pop("wt_deferred", None):
                self.save()   # owned (WHARF_KEYS), so save() drops it: the block's next new worktree waits again
            return True
        if t.get("wt_deferred"):
            return True
        t["wt_deferred"] = helmlib.now()
        self.save()
        return False

    def ensure_trusted(self, env):
        """The picked login must have trusted this repo before its claude starts: an interactive
        session in an untrusted folder stops at the trust dialog for a person, which no one is there
        to answer on the yard (S1 probe: four starts of 90 s each, all at the picked login's dialog). Dispatch
        has done the same since 2026-10-13 (`ensure_trusted`, bin/dispatch): `dispatch-rc trusted` asks,
        lighthouse's `trust-projects` writes what the dialog would for the login's config dir, and it is
        read back once. Still untrusted is a failed start, never a try at the dialog itself."""
        d = (env or {}).get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or ""

        def trusted():
            try:
                return subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(HERE / "dispatch-rc"), "trusted", str(self.repo), "--config-dir", d],
                                      capture_output=True, timeout=60).returncode == 0
            except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
                return False   # unread is untrusted: a Refused below, settled as a failed start, never a stray exception
        if trusted():
            return
        found = common.tool("trust-projects")   # lighthouse's, found through the core
        tp = shlex.split(os.environ.get("WHARF_TRUST") or "") or ([sys.executable, str(found)] if found else [])   # WHARF_TRUST: tests
        if not tp:
            raise Refused("untrusted: %s is not trusted by %s and trust-projects is not installed" % (self.repo, d or "the default login"), 1)
        tenv = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR"}
        if d:
            tenv["CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR"] = d
        try:
            subprocess.run(tp, env=tenv, capture_output=True, timeout=120)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            pass
        if not trusted():
            raise Refused("untrusted after trust-projects (%s)" % (d or "the default login"), 1)

    def start_orca(self, st, task, run, coord):
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        h, o = harness(), orca()
        # Orca puts a Task whose worker exited back to `ready`: a start is counted, never looped —
        # the first one and the block's own retries (0–2), then the plan says failed (spent())
        ctx = h.Ctx()
        model, effort = blueprintlib.run_of(s)   # a principal tier's own, where the block names none
        req = {"agent": s.get("agent") or "claude", "model": model, "effort": effort,
               "account": "auto", "ship": self.bp["name"], "repo": str(self.repo)}
        # on another host the worker runs on the login that host's Orca holds: a pick here would name
        # a login dir of this Mac, and Orca has no login per worker (orca.start(on=))
        on = blueprintlib.remote_host(s, self.here)
        try:
            login = o._login(ctx, req, req["agent"]) if req["agent"] == "claude" and not on else (None, {})
            path, br = self.remote_worktree(st, on) if on else self.worktree(st)
            if not on and not self.worktree_known(st, path):
                if _cache.get("tick"):
                    _cache["tick"] -= 1   # nothing started: the tick's slot goes back (start() took it)
                return "not started: worktree not yet known to Orca (retried next pass)"
            e, crash = self.intent("worker-start", sid, task=task)
            try:
                if req["agent"] == "claude" and not on:
                    self.ensure_trusted(login[1])   # a refusal is a failed start, counted: it is settled below
                did, res, own = o.start(ctx, req, "path:%s" % path, run, coord, login, task=task,
                                        term_title=br.rsplit("/", 1)[-1], on=on)
            except (h.Failed, Refused) as x:
                # raised before Orca made a Dispatch (a login terminal, the agent's wait): settled,
                # so the next apply reads no crash; still a try (a start that keeps failing stops)
                self.settle(e, crash, None, str(x))
                raise
            self.settle(e, crash, {"id": did}, None if did else res)
        except (h.Failed, Refused) as x:
            return "not started: %s" % x
        if not did:
            return "not started: %s" % res
        t = self.task(sid)
        t.setdefault("orca_dispatches", [])
        if did not in t["orca_dispatches"]:
            t["orca_dispatches"].append(did)
        self.save()
        where = " on " + on if on else ""
        report(self.pid, sid, "running", "Orca dispatch %s in %s%s" % (did, path, where), branch=br)
        return "started dispatch %s on %s%s (login %s)" % (did, br, where, login[0] or ("%s's Orca's own" % on if on else "Orca's own"))

    def start_claude_code(self, st, task, run, coord):
        """The section as a seeded brief on the block's branch, started by dispatch (bin/pickup seed,
        which commits docs/handoff/<date>-<topic>.md and starts it); Orca's Task mirrors it."""
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        brief = Path(self.p.get("dir") or helmlib.plan_dir(self.pid)) / ("brief-%s.md" % sid)
        brief.write_text("# %s — block of ship %s\n%s\n" % (sid, self.bp["name"], blueprintlib.spec_of(self.bp, st)))
        argv = [str(HERE / "pickup"), "seed", sid, "--file", str(brief), "--repo", str(self.repo), "--no-blueprint"]   # the block is this ship's: no one-block ship of its own (S5)
        if s.get("account"):
            argv += ["--account", s["account"]]
        e, crash = self.intent("seed", sid)
        # DISPATCH_SHIP (and DISPATCH_PLAN until rename S8): the seeded session reports to this ship,
        # wherever wharf runs (launchd has no session id)
        # (no DISPATCH_TASK: a caller that is itself a block must not make this start read as that block's
        # own `--next`, which `wharf next` would swallow)
        env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "DISPATCH_TASK"}
        env.update(helmlib.env_pairs("ship", self.pid))
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=SESSION_START, env=env)
            rc, out = r.returncode, (r.stdout or "")
            tail = ((r.stderr or "") + out).strip()[-300:]
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as x:
            # what it printed before the kill still names the branch it made
            out = x.stdout.decode(errors="replace") if isinstance(x.stdout, bytes) else (x.stdout or "")
            rc, tail = 124, "pickup seed timed out after %ds" % SESSION_START
        m = re.search(r"seeded (claude/\S+)", out)
        # a seed is made once: a failed one that made its branch is not seeded again (the topic is open)
        self.settle(e, crash, {"id": m.group(1) if m else None}, None if (rc == 0 or m) else tail)
        if m:
            self.task(sid)["seeded_branch"] = m.group(1)
            self.task(sid)["branch"] = m.group(1)
            self.save()
        if rc and not m:
            return "not started: pickup seed: %s" % tail[-200:]
        # seed prints its start lines and exits 0 where it starts nothing (launch_seed's other kinds)
        hand = [x.strip() for x in out.splitlines() if x.strip().startswith(("start it", "nothing started"))
                or "press Enter there" in x or "dispatch refused it" in x]
        if rc or hand:
            report(self.pid, sid, "waiting", "seeded %s, not started: %s" % (m.group(1) if m else sid, (hand or [tail])[0][:200]))
            return "raised: seeded %s, not started — %s" % (m.group(1) if m else sid, (hand or [tail])[0][:160])
        # Orca's Task stays `ready`: `dispatched` needs an Orca Dispatch (task_not_startable). The
        # settled seed line says it started (started()); the plan's end completes the Task.
        report(self.pid, sid, "running", "dispatched as %s" % (m.group(1) if m else sid))
        return "seeded and dispatched %s" % (m.group(1) if m else sid)

    def start_shell(self, st, task, run, coord):
        """The command in the repo's main checkout, `<wt>` the worktree of the block's one
        predecessor with a branch; the Task `dispatched` first, so a crash mid-command is never
        run again blindly (dangling(): it fails the Task instead)."""
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        if s.get("launch") == "finish":
            ended = self.launch_on_main(st)
            if ended:
                return ended
            if self.launch is not None:
                return self.start_launch(st, task)
            said = "launch: finish — %s's /finish launches it (a gate file is in it)" % (skipper(self.bp, self.pid) or "the skipper")
            if not self.dry and (plan_status(self.pid).get(sid) or {}).get("progress") != said:
                report(self.pid, sid, "waiting", said)
            return "raised: launch: finish is the skipper's (%s)" % (skipper(self.bp, self.pid) or "none named")
        cmd = s["command"]
        if "<wt>" in cmd:
            wts = [w for w in (self.wt_of(d) for d in st["deps"]) if w]
            if len(wts) != 1:
                return "not started: <wt> needs exactly one predecessor with a worktree (has %d)" % len(wts)
            cmd = cmd.replace("<wt>", shlex.quote(str(wts[0])))
        # no `dispatched` first: Orca refuses it without an active Dispatch (task_not_startable, live
        # 2026-10-17), so the ledger's line is what keeps a crashed command from running again
        e, crash = self.intent("shell", sid, task=task)
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(["sh", "-c", cmd], cwd=str(self.repo), capture_output=True, text=True,
                               timeout=int(s.get("timeout_seconds") or SHELL_TIMEOUT))
            rc, tail = r.returncode, ((r.stdout or "") + (r.stderr or "")).strip()[-400:]
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            rc, tail = 124, "timed out after %ss" % (s.get("timeout_seconds") or SHELL_TIMEOUT)
        self.settle(e, crash, {"id": str(rc)})
        status = "completed" if rc == 0 else "failed"
        _, err = self.call("task-update", sid, ["orchestration", "task-update", "--id", task, "--status", status,
                                                "--result", "exit %d: %s" % (rc, tail or "no output"), "--run", run, "--from", coord])
        report(self.pid, sid, None if rc == 0 else "failed", "shell exit %d%s" % (rc, (": " + tail.splitlines()[-1][:120]) if tail else ""))
        return "ran `%s`: exit %d%s" % (cmd, rc, (" (task-update: %s)" % err) if err else "")

    # -- a settled builder ----------------------------------------------------------------------

    def built_before_retry(self, st, task):
        """An Orca block Orca put back to `ready` after its worker ended (an exit, a stop): its
        done_when read before a retry. When it holds in the block's worktree the work is done — the
        plan says done, the builder is released, nothing starts (rename S3, 2026-10-19: built and
        committed, a retry would have built it again). None when it does not hold, or there was no
        start to retry, or the block names no done_when: today's retry stands."""
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        if s.get("provider") != "orca" or not s.get("done_when"):
            return None
        ran = [e for e in self.rec.get("ledger") or [] if e.get("block") == sid and e.get("op") == "worker-start"
               and e.get("state") != "failed" and e.get("task") in (None, task)]
        if not ran:
            return None
        ok, what = self.done_when(st)
        if not ok:
            return None
        did = ((self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(sid) or {}).get("orca_dispatches") or [ran[-1].get("id")]
        if self.dry:
            return "built: %s holds — would end it, not start it again" % what
        report(self.pid, sid, "done", "built; the worker ended with no report (dispatch %s): %s" % (did[-1], what))
        self.did += ["%s: %s" % (sid, x) for x in self.release_builder(st)]
        return "built: %s holds — ended, not started again" % what

    # -- work already on main: never rebuilt (skipper-resilience S9) ---------------------------------

    SIBLING = "a sibling may have built this"
    SHARED = {"AGENTS.md", "CLAUDE.md", "TODO.md", "CHANGELOG.md"}   # read (4)'s default paths leave them out

    def branches_mod(self):
        """wharf's branches.py (the proof `bin/pr` carries a branch by), through the core's tool lookup;
        None when wharf is not here: the reads that need it are then no hit."""
        if "branches" not in _cache:
            path = common.tool("branches.py")
            try:
                _cache["branches"] = _mod("branches", path) if path else None
            except Exception as x:  # noqa: BLE001 — a file mid-edit, or a core it cannot find: no reads, never a dead apply
                self.onmain_log("branches.py: %s" % x)
                _cache["branches"] = None
        return _cache["branches"]

    def onmain_log(self, text):
        """One line on stderr for a read that could not be made, once per process: the reads only
        prevent duplicate work, so a failure is "no hit" and never holds a start back."""
        said = _cache.setdefault("onmain_said", set())
        if text not in said:
            said.add(text)
            print("wharf: on-main reads: %s" % text, file=sys.stderr)

    def main_ref(self):
        """`origin/<main>` after one `git fetch origin <main>` per pass, or None: no origin (nothing to
        read), no branches.py, or a fetch that failed (said once). A dry run fetches nothing and reads
        the ref as it stands."""
        cache = _cache.setdefault("onmain", {})
        key = str(self.repo)
        if key in cache:
            return cache[key]
        ref, bm = None, self.branches_mod()
        if bm and _git(self.repo, "config", "--get", "remote.origin.url"):
            main = bm.main_branch(self.repo)
            ok = True
            if not self.dry:
                env = dict(os.environ, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT="0")
                # never over the caller's own ssh command (the variable outranks core.sshCommand)
                if not env.get("GIT_SSH_COMMAND") and not _git(self.repo, "config", "--get", "core.sshCommand"):
                    env["GIT_SSH_COMMAND"] = "ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=15"
                try:
                    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(self.repo), "fetch", "-q", "origin", main], capture_output=True,
                                       text=True, timeout=60, env=env)
                    ok = r.returncode == 0
                    if not ok:
                        self.onmain_log("git fetch origin %s failed (%s)" % (main, (r.stderr or "").strip()[-120:]))
                except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as x:
                    ok = False
                    self.onmain_log("git fetch origin %s: %s" % (main, type(x).__name__))
            if ok and _git(self.repo, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "origin/%s^{commit}" % main):
                ref = "origin/%s" % main
        cache[key] = ref
        return ref

    def branch_obj(self, br, archived=False):
        """The branch as branches.prove reads one (it asks for `.tips`): its tips, local and on origin, each
        with its ref; None when neither exists. `archived` reads sync's `refs/archive/…` copies too: a
        landed branch is archived at the next session start."""
        if not br or not self.branches_mod():
            return None
        refs = ["refs/heads/%s" % br, "refs/remotes/origin/%s" % br]
        if archived:
            refs += ["refs/archive/%s" % br, "refs/archive/origin/%s" % br]
        refs = [(r, _git(self.repo, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "%s^{commit}" % r)) for r in refs]
        refs = [(r, sha) for r, sha in refs if sha]
        if not refs:
            return None
        return types.SimpleNamespace(name=br, refs=refs, tips=sorted({sha for _, sha in refs}))

    def own_work(self, b, ref):
        """Whether a branch holds work of its own. A tip that is not on main has commits main lacks. A
        tip that is an ancestor of main is either merged or a branch cut from main and never written to,
        and branches.prove cannot tell them apart: a local branch with a `commit` entry in its reflog (a
        commit, an amend, a merge concluded by commit) whose commit the tip still holds was written to; a
        rebase, a fast-forward or a rename onto a newer main is not a commit, and a commit a reset took
        away (a skipper forcing a rebuild) no longer counts, so neither is read as merged. A tip on origin
        alone that main holds is not counted: its reflog says nothing of who wrote it."""
        def anc(a, b):
            return not subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(self.repo), "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", a, b],
                                      capture_output=True).returncode
        for name, tip in b.refs:
            if not anc(tip, ref):
                return True
            if name.startswith("refs/heads/"):
                for x in (_git(self.repo, "reflog", "show", "--format=%H %gs", name) or "").splitlines():
                    sha, _, what = x.partition(" ")
                    if what.startswith("commit") and anc(sha, tip):
                        return True
        return False

    def on_main(self, st, task):
        """Work already on main is never built again: read before a block starts and before a retry of
        one, cheapest first, after one fetch of origin/<main> a pass. Returns the line (`launched via
        <sha>` / `launched via #N`: the block is ended; `raised: a sibling may have built this (<sha>)`:
        the skipper decides), or None, today's start. (1) done_when's file or marker on origin/<main>;
        (2) a merged PR whose head is the block's branch; (3) the branch's changed files all identical
        on main (branches.prove, bin/pr's proof for a carried branch); (4), before the first start only,
        the owned paths moved on main by a commit of no block of this ship. A read that cannot be made is
        no hit, with a line said once. Blocks that build (an Orca worker, a seeded session) only."""
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        if st["kind"] != "block" or s.get("provider") not in ("orca", "claude-code") or s.get("launch"):
            return None
        left = time_left()
        if left is not None and left < 120:
            return None   # the fetch and the API are not worth the start's own seconds
        try:
            ref = self.main_ref()
        except Exception as x:  # noqa: BLE001
            self.onmain_log("main_ref: %s" % x)
            ref = None
        if not ref:
            return None
        op = "worker-start" if s["provider"] == "orca" else "seed"
        ran = [e for e in self.rec.get("ledger") or [] if e.get("block") == sid and e.get("op") == op
               and e.get("state") != "failed" and (op == "seed" or e.get("task") in (None, task))]
        for read in (self.read_done_when_main, self.read_merged_pr, self.read_proved):
            try:
                hit = read(st, ref)
            except Exception as x:  # noqa: BLE001 — a read that breaks is no hit
                self.onmain_log("%s: %s" % (read.__name__, x))
                hit = None
            if hit:
                how, what = hit
                if self.dry:
                    return "%s — %s: would end it, not start it" % (how, what)
                report(self.pid, sid, "launched", how)
                # what launch_on_main reads: a block these reads ended, not one a launch landed
                self.task(sid)["on_main"] = how
                self.save()
                if ran:   # before a first start no builder of this ship ran: a lock there is someone else's
                    self.did += ["%s: %s" % (sid, x) for x in self.release_builder(st)]
                return "%s — %s: ended, not started" % (how, what)
        if ran:
            return None
        try:
            return self.read_sibling(st, ref)
        except Exception as x:  # noqa: BLE001
            self.onmain_log("read_sibling: %s" % x)
            return None

    def dw_parts(self, st):
        """(kind, value, path) of a block's done_when when it is a `file` or a `marker` (the two a blob can
        answer), else None. `check` and `memo_answered` need a worktree and are skipped."""
        dw = st["raw"].get("done_when")
        if not isinstance(dw, dict) or len(dw) != 1:
            return None
        (k, v), = dw.items()
        if k not in ("file", "marker") or not isinstance(v, str):
            return None
        path = v.partition("#")[0] if k == "marker" else v
        if not path or path.startswith("/") or ".." in path.split("/"):
            return None
        return k, v, path

    def dw_holds(self, st, rev):
        """Whether the block's done_when (file or marker) holds in the tree of `rev` (`git cat-file -e`,
        then the blob); None when it is neither kind."""
        parts = self.dw_parts(st)
        if not parts:
            return None
        k, v, path = parts
        if _git(self.repo, "cat-file", "-e", "%s:%s" % (rev, path)) is None:
            return False
        if k == "marker":
            text = _git(self.repo, "show", "%s:%s" % (rev, path))
            return text is not None and marker_built(text.splitlines(), v.partition("#")[2])
        return True

    def main_at_created(self, ref):
        """origin/<main> as it stood when the plan was made (first parents only: a merged side branch's
        older commit was never main's state), or None."""
        created = self.p.get("created")
        return _git(self.repo, "rev-list", "-1", "--first-parent", "--before=%d" % math.ceil(created), ref) if created else None

    def read_done_when_main(self, st, ref):
        """(1) done_when's `file` or `marker` read from origin/<main>: (`launched via <sha>`, what) of the
        commit that last touched it, else None. Not evidence when it already held on main when the plan was
        made (a path that always existed, a marker line that only describes the work): the block starts as
        today. A marker counts only against its doc as it stood on main then: a doc that landed later
        (a ship laid from its design branch) may say "built" of a step that is not started."""
        parts = self.dw_parts(st)
        if not parts or not self.dw_holds(st, ref):
            return None
        k, v, path = parts
        base = self.main_at_created(ref)
        if k == "marker" and (not base or _git(self.repo, "cat-file", "-e", "%s:%s" % (base, path)) is None):
            return None
        if base and self.dw_holds(st, base):
            return None
        sha = _git(self.repo, "log", "-1", "--format=%h", ref, "--", path) or _git(self.repo, "rev-parse", "--short", ref)
        return "launched via %s" % sha, "done_when %s %s is on %s" % (k, v, ref)

    def read_merged_pr(self, st, ref):
        """(2) a merged pull request whose head is the block's branch (GitHub, `common.api` on the pulls
        list: `merged_at` set): (`launched via #N`, what) or None. A PR closed unmerged (rename S5's #428)
        is no hit, and neither is an answer that never came. While the branch is still here, the PR's
        head must be one of its tips (common.merged_pr's rule): a branch that went on committing after
        its PR merged, or a name reused for later work, has work no PR landed."""
        if os.environ.get("PLAN_NO_GH") or self.dry:
            return None
        br = self.branch(st)
        slug = common.repo_slug(_git(self.repo, "config", "--get", "remote.origin.url") or "")
        if not br or not slug:
            return None
        from urllib.parse import quote
        status, prs = common.api("GET", "/repos/%s/pulls?state=closed&per_page=10&head=%s:%s"
                                 % (slug, slug.split("/")[0], quote(br, safe="")))
        if status != 200 or not isinstance(prs, list):
            self.onmain_log("GitHub's pulls list for %s gave %s" % (br, status or "no answer"))
            return None
        # the newest tip: the local branch where there is one (origin's ref is as old as the last push)
        b = self.branch_obj(br)
        newest = (dict(b.refs).get("refs/heads/%s" % br) or b.refs[0][1]) if b else None
        for pr in prs:
            if not isinstance(pr, dict):
                continue
            head = pr.get("head") or {}
            if pr.get("merged_at") and head.get("ref") == br and pr.get("number") \
                    and (newest is None or head.get("sha") == newest):
                return "launched via #%s" % pr["number"], "its PR #%s merged" % pr["number"]
        return None

    def read_proved(self, st, ref):
        """(3) the content proof of a worker block's branch (prove_branch); when its done_when is a file or
        a marker, it must hold at one of the branch's tips too: a branch that never made the thing it was
        to make is not proved by files that are the predecessors' own."""
        b = self.branch_obj(self.branch(st))
        if b is not None and self.dw_parts(st) and not any(self.dw_holds(st, tip) for tip in b.tips):
            return None
        return self.prove_branch(self.branch(st), self.wt_of(st["id"]), ref)

    def prove_branch(self, br, wt, ref):
        """(`launched via <sha>`, what) when every file the branch changed is identical on origin/<main>, or
        its tips are merged into it (branches.prove): not for a branch with nothing of its own (own_work),
        nor one whose commits net to nothing (branches.prove's vacuous "no net change": nothing was built),
        nor while its worktree holds uncommitted work (the proof speaks for commits only)."""
        bm = self.branches_mod()
        b = self.branch_obj(br)
        if b is None or not self.own_work(b, ref):
            return None
        if wt and bm.uncommitted(wt) != 0:
            return None   # uncommitted work, or git could not say
        proof = bm.prove(self.repo, b, ref)
        if not proof or "no net change" in proof:
            return None
        return "launched via %s" % _git(self.repo, "rev-parse", "--short", ref), "%s on %s (%s)" % (b.name, ref, proof)

    def launch_on_main(self, st):
        """A `launch: finish` block with nothing left to land: every predecessor was ended by the on-main
        reads (the task's `on_main`, never the progress text: a launch's own landing says `launched via
        #N` too) and it names no branch of its own, or its one branch is proved on origin/<main> (read 3,
        the #442 shape: a branch carried across by another's PR, with none of its own). Reported
        `launched`; None otherwise, and every earlier path of the launch stands. The line, or None."""
        deps = st["deps"]
        ps = plan_status(self.pid)
        how = [(self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(d, {}).get("on_main") for d in deps]
        hit = None
        # the flag counts while the reads' report is still the latest: a block reopened and rebuilt since
        # reports again, and its rebuild is the launch's to land
        if deps and not st["raw"].get("branch") and all((ps.get(d) or {}).get("status") in ENDED and h
                                                         and str((ps.get(d) or {}).get("progress") or "") == h for d, h in zip(deps, how)):
            hit = (how[0], "its predecessor%s already on main" % ("s are" if len(deps) > 1 else " is"))
        else:
            try:
                brs = [st["raw"]["branch"]] if st["raw"].get("branch") else [b for b in (self.branch(self.bp["by_id"][d]) for d in deps) if b]
                ref = self.main_ref() if len(brs) == 1 else None
                hit = self.prove_branch(brs[0], self.launch_wt(st), ref) if ref else None
            except Exception as x:  # noqa: BLE001
                self.onmain_log("launch_on_main: %s" % x)
        if not hit:
            return None
        how, what = hit
        if self.dry:
            return "%s — %s: would end it" % (how, what)
        report(self.pid, st["id"], "launched", how)
        return "%s — %s: ended" % (how, what)

    def block_sessions(self):
        """The session ids of this ship's blocks, from the plan's reports."""
        return {str(t.get("session")) for sid, t in plan_status(self.pid).items() if sid in self.bp["by_id"] and t.get("session")}

    def own_commit_ids(self, ref):
        """(shas, patch ids) of what this ship's own block branches hold: /finish rewrites a branch and drops
        its trailers, so a commit that landed from one of them is told by its patch. A branch sync has
        archived is read from `refs/archive/…` (launched, gone on GitHub, or empty: an empty one's range
        may hold main's own commits, which only errs toward no raise); a tip already on main has its
        commits since the plan was made. Once a pass, per ship."""
        key = (self.pid, self.bp["name"], str(self.repo))
        cache = _cache.setdefault("onmain_own", {})
        if key in cache:
            return cache[key]
        shas, ids, base = set(), set(), self.main_at_created(ref)
        for st in self.bp["blocks"]:
            if st["kind"] != "block" or st["raw"].get("provider") not in ("orca", "claude-code"):
                continue
            b = self.branch_obj(self.branch(st), archived=True)
            live = [(n, t) for n, t in (b.refs if b else []) if not n.startswith("refs/archive/")]
            if b is None or (live and not self.own_work(types.SimpleNamespace(refs=live), ref)):
                continue
            for tip in b.tips:
                shas.add(tip)
                mb = _git(self.repo, "merge-base", ref, tip)
                if mb == tip:   # on main already: the range from the merge base is empty
                    mb = base
                for c in (_git(self.repo, "rev-list", "--no-merges", "%s..%s" % (mb, tip)) or "").split() if mb else []:
                    got = self.patch_id(c)
                    if got:
                        ids.add(got)
        cache[key] = (shas, ids)
        return shas, ids

    def patch_id(self, sha):
        try:
            d = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(self.repo), "diff-tree", "-p", "--root", "--no-ext-diff", sha],
                               capture_output=True, timeout=30)
            r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(self.repo), "patch-id", "--stable"], input=d.stdout, capture_output=True, timeout=30)
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
            return None
        return r.stdout.split()[0].decode() if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.split() else None

    def read_sibling(self, st, ref):
        """(4) before the first start: the paths this block owns (`owns:`, else the files its predecessors'
        branches changed) moved on origin/<main> since the plan was made, by a commit of no block of this
        ship (no `Claude-Session` trailer of one of its sessions, and not the patch of one of its branches'
        own commits). Raised to the skipper, once: `waiting`, with the commit's sha. The skipper closes the
        block (`helm report --status launched`) or clears it (any later report, `--status planned`); a later
        stranger raises again."""
        sid, created, bm = st["id"], self.p.get("created"), self.branches_mod()
        if not created:
            return None
        paths = [x for x in (st["raw"].get("owns") or []) if isinstance(x, str) and x.strip() and not x.startswith("/")
                 and ".." not in x.split("/")]
        if not paths:
            for d in st["deps"]:
                dst = self.bp["by_id"].get(d)
                b = self.branch_obj(self.branch(dst), archived=True) if dst and dst["kind"] == "block" else None
                for tip in (b.tips if b else []):
                    mb = _git(self.repo, "merge-base", ref, tip)
                    paths += (bm.changed_paths(self.repo, mb, tip) or []) if mb else []
            # files every landing touches say nothing of who built this block
            paths = [x for x in paths if x.rsplit("/", 1)[-1] not in self.SHARED and not x.startswith(".helloworld/")]
        paths = sorted(set(paths))
        if not paths:
            return None
        # rounded up to the second: git compares whole seconds, and a commit in the second the plan was made
        # in, made before it, is not a sibling's
        since = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z", time.localtime(math.ceil(created)))
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(self.repo), "log", ref, "--no-merges", "--since=" + since,
                            "--format=%H%x1f%B%x1e", "--"] + paths, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
        if r.returncode:
            return None
        mine, theirs = self.block_sessions(), None
        strangers = []
        for rec in r.stdout.split("\x1e"):
            sha, _, msg = rec.strip().partition("\x1f")
            if not sha:
                continue
            marks = re.findall(r"^Claude-Session:\s*(\S+)\s*$", msg, re.M)
            if any(m.startswith(v) or v.startswith(m) for m in marks for v in mine):
                continue
            if theirs is None:
                theirs = self.own_commit_ids(ref)
            if sha in theirs[0] or self.patch_id(sha) in theirs[1]:
                continue
            strangers.append(sha[:7])
            break   # one is enough to ask
        if not strangers:
            return None
        sha, t = strangers[0], self.task(sid)
        said = "%s (%s)" % (self.SIBLING, sha)
        cur = plan_status(self.pid).get(sid) or {}
        if sha in (t.get("sibling_seen") or []):
            if cur.get("status") == "waiting" and str(cur.get("progress") or "").startswith(self.SIBLING):
                return "raised: " + said   # still the skipper's
            return None   # cleared (the skipper's later report)
        if not self.dry:
            # the report first: a pass killed between the two then asks twice, never reads a raise
            # nobody saw as cleared
            report(self.pid, sid, "waiting", said)
            t.setdefault("sibling_seen", []).append(sha)
            self.save()
        return "raised: " + said

    def release_builder(self, st):
        """A block the yard has ended: its worktree's lock marked handed over (owner.json's
        `handover`, the field `pickup next` writes: the next writer takes it), and Orca asked to stop
        the worker. Every session runs the Session-tab waiter, so a finished builder reads `shell`
        and its lock would refuse the launch's /finish (bin/autofinish-run's lock_refusal);
        `worker-stop` answers `processAction: none` for these terminals (2026-10-19), so the handover
        is what frees the launch. A lock a launch holds is left alone. Lines of what was done."""
        if self.dry or st["raw"].get("provider") != "orca":
            return []
        out, sid = [], st["id"]
        wt = self.wt_of(sid)
        gd = _git(wt, "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir") if wt and wt.is_dir() else None
        if gd:
            state = Path(gd) / "claude"
            lock = core().read_owner(state)
            launch_state = read_json(state / "autofinish.json") or {}
            if lock and lock.get("session") and not lock.get("handover") and \
                    not (launch_state.get("session") == lock["session"] and not launch_state.get("ended")):
                try:
                    core().write_owner(state, lock["session"], lock.get("branch") or self.branch(st), handover=time.time())
                    out.append("lock handed over (session %s)" % str(lock["session"])[:8])
                except OSError as e:
                    out.append("lock not handed over: %s" % e)
        t = self.task(sid)
        for did in (t.get("orca_dispatches") or [])[-1:]:
            if did in (t.get("stopped") or []):
                continue
            res, err = self.call("worker-stop", sid, ["orchestration", "worker-stop", "--dispatch", did], timeout=60)
            if not err:   # a failed ask is asked again at the next pass
                t.setdefault("stopped", []).append(did)
                self.save()
            act = orca()._first(res or {}, "processAction", "stop.processAction", "worker.processAction")
            out.append("worker-stop %s: %s" % (did, err or ("processAction %s" % act if act else "asked")))
        return out

    # -- the launch (--launch) -------------------------------------------------------------------

    def launch_wt(self, st):
        """The worktree a `launch: finish` block launches: its own branch's, else its one predecessor's."""
        wt = self.wt_of(st["id"]) if st["raw"].get("branch") else None
        if wt and wt.is_dir():
            return wt
        wts = [w for w in (self.wt_of(d) for d in st["deps"]) if w and w.is_dir()]
        return wts[0] if len(wts) == 1 else None

    def pr_state(self, br):
        """(merged?, PR number or None) of a branch, from GitHub (`gh pr view`); (None, why) when not asked."""
        if os.environ.get("PLAN_NO_GH"):
            return None, "GitHub not asked (PLAN_NO_GH)"
        if self.dry:
            return None, "GitHub not asked in a dry run"
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(["gh", "pr", "view", br, "--json", "state,number"], cwd=str(self.repo),
                               capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
            d = json.loads(r.stdout or "{}")
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ValueError) as e:
            return None, "gh %s" % type(e).__name__
        return d.get("state") == "MERGED", d.get("number")

    def launches_running(self):
        """Launches under way in this repo now, from each worktree's `claude/autofinish.json`: started,
        not ended, and its waiter alive (`autofinish-waiter.json`) or started under 10 min ago (its
        child may not have written the waiter yet). A dead runner's state is not counted."""
        gd = _git(self.repo, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir")
        if not gd:
            return 0
        return sum(1 for f in [Path(gd) / "claude"] + sorted(Path(gd).glob("worktrees/*/claude"))
                   if not (read_json(f / "autofinish.json") or {"ended": True}).get("ended") and launch_live(f))

    def runs_busy(self, wt):
        """(runs busy on this Mac, dispatch's cap) as dispatch counts them before a start
        (`dispatch-rc live --no-reap`: read only; warm and waiting runs not counted), or (None, cap)
        when it cannot be read — then the start goes ahead and dispatch's own refusal decides. A
        launch refused there ends `never-started` at gate `refused` and is started again here. The
        cap is dispatch's `--cap` (its one home; DISPATCH_MAX_RUNS first, as dispatch reads it)."""
        try:
            most = int(os.environ.get("DISPATCH_MAX_RUNS") or subprocess.run(
                [str(HERE / "dispatch"), "--cap"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30).stdout.strip())
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ValueError):
            return None, None
        topic = re.sub(r"^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}-", "", Path(wt).name)
        try:
            r = subprocess.run([os.environ.get("WHARF_DISPATCH_RC") or str(HERE / "dispatch-rc"), "live", "--no-reap",
                                str(self.repo), topic], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
            return int(r.stdout.strip()), most
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ValueError):
            return None, most

    def start_launch(self, st, task):
        """--launch: a `launch: finish` block whose predecessor ended is launched by `bin/autofinish-run
        <wt> --session <the skipper's>` (a fresh /finish --unattended, every gate run), once the
        worktree's lock is free or handed over and fewer than --launches run in the repo. Its PR
        merged: reported `launched` by wharf itself. A launch that stopped on this tip: reported
        `waiting` with its gate, once — autofinish-run never retries a tip, and neither does this."""
        s, sid = st["raw"], st["id"]
        # the branch first, the worktree after: a launched branch's worktree may be gone already
        brs = [s["branch"]] if s.get("branch") else [b for b in (self.branch(self.bp["by_id"][d]) for d in st["deps"]) if b]
        merged, pr = self.pr_state(brs[0]) if len(brs) == 1 else (None, None)
        if merged:
            if not self.dry:
                report(self.pid, sid, "launched", "launched via #%s" % pr if pr else "its PR merged")
            return "launched: %s merged%s" % (brs[0], " (#%s)" % pr if pr else "")
        wt = self.launch_wt(st)
        if wt is None:
            return "not started: launch: finish needs its branch's worktree, or one predecessor's, on this Mac"
        br = _git(wt, "symbolic-ref", "--short", "-q", "HEAD") or brs[0]
        gd = _git(wt, "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir")
        state = Path(gd) / "claude" if gd else None
        tip = _git(wt, "rev-parse", "HEAD")
        af = read_json(state / "autofinish.json") if state else None
        last = (plan_status(self.pid).get(sid) or {}).get("progress")
        if af and not af.get("ended") and launch_live(state):
            # whatever the tip: /finish rewrites the branch as it goes
            return "raised: its launch runs (session %s, started %s)" % (str(af.get("session"))[:8], af.get("started"))
        if af and af.get("ended") and af.get("outcome") in core().LAUNCHED_OUTCOMES:
            return "raised: its /finish launched it%s; GitHub does not say merged yet (%s)" % (
                " (#%s)" % af["pr"] if af.get("pr") else "", pr or "asked")
        # refused before any session (dispatch's run cap: gate `refused`, `not-launched` before
        # 2026-10-17), or died: queued, never stopped — autofinish-run starts those again on the
        # same tip (its refusal()), and only those (review, 2026-10-19)
        refused = bool(af and af.get("ended") and (af.get("gate") in core().REFUSED_GATES or af.get("outcome") == "died"))
        if af and af.get("ended") and af.get("tip") == tip and not refused:
            said = "launch stopped: %s%s on %s — the skipper's" % (af.get("outcome") or "no outcome",
                                                                   " at gate %s" % af["gate"] if af.get("gate") else "", str(tip)[:7])
            if not self.dry and last != said:
                report(self.pid, sid, "waiting", said)
            return "raised: " + said
        lock = core().read_owner(state) if state else None
        holder = (lock or {}).get("session")
        me = (self.launch or {}).get("session")
        if holder and holder != me:
            # a dead holder frees it too: autofinish-run's own rule (its registry read) decides past this.
            # Its lock_refusal, mirrored: an idle holder frees it; handed over, `shell` too; busy, never
            import asklib
            rec = asklib.registry(holder)
            if rec and pid_alive(rec.get("pid")) and rec.get("status") != "idle":
                if not lock.get("handover"):
                    return "raised: waits for its lock (session %s holds it, live, not handed over)" % holder[:8]
                if rec.get("status") not in ("idle", "shell"):
                    return "raised: waits for its lock (session %s handed it over, still %s)" % (holder[:8], rec.get("status") or "with no status")
        n = (self.launch or {}).get("launches")
        cap = 2 if n is None else int(n)   # --launches 0 holds every launch
        running = self.launches_running()
        if running >= cap:
            return "raised: %d launch%s under way (--launches %d): it waits" % (running, "" if running == 1 else "es", cap)
        busy, most = self.runs_busy(wt)
        if busy is not None and busy >= most:
            return "raised: %s%d runs busy, dispatch's cap is %d (dispatch --status): the launch waits for one to end" % (
                "queued — its last start was refused by the run cap; " if refused else "", busy, most)
        call = self.merge_flags()
        argv = [os.environ.get("WHARF_AUTOFINISH_RUN") or str(HERE / "autofinish-run"), str(wt)] + (["--session", me] if me else []) + call
        if self.dry:
            return "would start the launch: %s" % " ".join(shlex.quote(x) for x in argv)
        e, crash = self.intent("launch", sid, task=task, tip=tip)
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300)
            rc, tail = r.returncode, ((r.stdout or "") + (r.stderr or "")).strip()
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as x:
            rc, tail = 124, str(x)
        self.settle(e, crash, {"id": tip}, None if rc == 0 else tail[-300:])
        if rc:
            return "not started: autofinish-run exit %d: %s" % (rc, (tail.splitlines() or [""])[-1][:200])
        how = (" " + " ".join(call[:3])) if call else ""
        report(self.pid, sid, "running", "launch started: autofinish-run %s%s" % (wt, how))
        return "started the launch of %s (autofinish-run%s%s)" % (br, how, ", session %s" % me[:8] if me else "")

    def merge_flags(self):
        """The landing call a yard launch carries (S6; the yard component's "The merge default"): the
        keel's merge as plan.json's `merge: {value, why}` records it (wharf apply --yard's
        merge_value) — yes: `--merge --by ship --digest <the pin's digest>`, which autofinish-run
        checks against the pinned copy and `laid_by` before it believes it; no, or nothing recorded
        (an unpinned ship the yard drives: no keel was asked), or no pinned digest: `--by ship --hold`, a ready PR
        for the owner's tap. --watch's launch (no `yard` in the dict) carries neither, as before."""
        if not (self.launch or {}).get("yard"):
            return []
        m = self.rec.get("merge") if isinstance(self.rec.get("merge"), dict) else {}
        pin = self.rec.get("pin") if isinstance(self.rec.get("pin"), dict) else {}
        if m.get("value") == "yes" and pin.get("digest"):
            return ["--merge", "--by", "ship", "--digest", pin["digest"]]
        return ["--by", "ship", "--hold"]   # the tick's own label: a hold launch is no person's override

    # -- a worker's question ---------------------------------------------------------------------

    def relay_questions(self, run, coord):
        """Each question a worker of this ship asked the coordinator and nobody has read (the orca
        adapter's questions(): `check --peek --types question`, never a consuming check), relayed
        once to the skipper with the block id and the text: the file queue its next prompt prints
        (hooks/ask_guard.py; asklib's file backend, bin/ask relay's road) when the skipper is live
        here, else the plan's `waiting` report the board shows. A `skipper: scope` ship's question is
        hailed to the scope's skipper while it holds the lease (skipper-resilience S6; S5 sent it by
        Talk): `hail <its session> --kind ask --when idle --no-file`, its page as HAIL_SPACE, a pointer
        (hail_question) — never the file road, which a scope skipper never reads, and the board when no
        road takes it or no live skipper holds the ship. Recorded in the ship's `relayed`,
        so a second pass never relays it again (rename S3's msg_5107b77a14a6 sat 30 min unread)."""
        if not run or not coord:
            return []
        qs = orca().questions(None, run, coord)
        if qs is None:
            return [("orca", "failed", None, "the Run's questions unread (check --peek)")]
        sk = self.scope_skipper()
        scoped = (self.bp["meta"].get("skipper") or self.bp["meta"].get("manager")) == "scope"
        st_now = plan_status(self.pid)
        by_did = {d: sid for sid, t in (self.p.get("tasks") or {}).items() if sid in self.bp["by_id"]
                  for d in t.get("orca_dispatches") or []}
        seen = set(self.rec.get("relayed") or [])
        rows = []
        for q in qs:
            sid = by_did.get(q.get("dispatch"))
            if not sid or q["id"] in seen or (st_now.get(sid) or {}).get("status") in ENDED:
                continue
            text = " ".join(str(q.get("text") or "").split())
            line = ("ASK %s %s/%s — Orca question %s from dispatch %s: %s — reply: orca orchestration reply --id %s "
                    "--body \"<text>\" --run %s --from %s" % (self.bp["meta"]["repo"], self.bp["name"], sid, q["id"],
                                                           q.get("dispatch"), text[:500], q["id"], run, coord))
            if self.dry:
                rows.append(("orca", "relay", sid, "would %s question %s to %s" % (
                    ("hail", q["id"], sk["name"]) if sk else ("relay", q["id"], skipper(self.bp, self.pid) or "the board"))))
                continue
            import asklib
            who = skipper(self.bp, self.pid)
            if scoped:
                # a `skipper: scope` ship's holder is its scope's skipper, which hears its inbox and its
                # `ask listen`, never a file line (S5's fifth finish review): hailed while it holds the
                # lease (sk), else the board, whoever holds it — the yard, a lapsed lease
                left = time_left()
                if sk and left is not None and left < HAIL_TIMEOUT + 30:
                    # a kill mid-hail would leave it unrecorded and hailed twice: the next pass asks
                    rows.append(("orca", "relay", sid, "question %s: not hailed — %ds before the tick's kill time" % (q["id"], max(0, left))))
                    continue
                if sk:
                    verdict, detail, road = self.hail_question(sk, sid, q, run, coord)
                    if verdict in HAIL_TAKEN:
                        if road == "subs":
                            # a subscription the fulfil may yet drop (its target ended, 72 h): carded too,
                            # so the question is never lost to a row nobody reads
                            report(self.pid, sid, "waiting", "Orca question %s: hailed once %s is idle" % (q["id"], sk["name"]))
                        verdict, detail = "hailed", "%s (%s)" % (sk["name"], detail)
                    else:
                        verdict, detail = "none", "the hail to %s was not taken: %s" % (sk["name"], detail)
                else:
                    verdict, detail = "none", "no live skipper holds the ship's lease"
            else:
                name, verdict, detail, _ = asklib.relay({"manager": who, "session": None, "plan": self.pid}, line, ["file"])
            if verdict == "hailed":
                how = "hailed to %s" % detail
            elif verdict == "queued":
                how = "the skipper's next prompt (%s)" % detail
            else:
                report(self.pid, sid, "waiting", "Orca question %s: %s" % (q["id"], text[:200]))
                how = "the board, as waiting (%s)" % detail
            self.rec.setdefault("relayed", []).append(q["id"])
            self.save()
            rows.append(("orca", "relay", sid, "question %s → %s" % (q["id"], how)))
        return rows

    def scope_skipper(self):
        """The skipper a `skipper: scope` ship's questions are hailed to, or None: the live skipper of
        the scope the ship's lease names (helm's asklib.scope_skipper: S5's `<host>-<scope>.json`, its pid
        and its session's registry pid alive), and only while it is the lease's holder (skipper()) — the
        yard's hold or a lapsed lease hails nobody. {session, name, space}. Read once per pass; a
        ship with a named skipper has none here (its file relay, as before)."""
        if (self.bp["meta"].get("skipper") or self.bp["meta"].get("manager")) != "scope":
            return None
        who = skipper(self.bp, self.pid)
        if not who:
            return None
        try:
            import asklib
            sm = asklib.scope_skipper(self.pid)
        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — a record that will not read is no skipper here
            return None
        if not sm or sm.get("manager") != who:
            return None
        return {"session": who, "name": sm.get("manager_name") or "the scope's skipper", "space": sm.get("space")}

    def question_pointer(self, sid, q, run, coord):
        """The hail's text: where the question is and how to answer it, never the worker's words — a
        hail is a pointer (its K13, 400 characters), and the question's text is Orca's to show. The read
        clause goes first when it does not fit; None when even the bare pointer does not."""
        head = "Orca question %s from %s/%s in plan %s (dispatch %s)" % (q["id"], self.bp["name"], sid, self.pid, q.get("dispatch"))
        read = " — read: orca orchestration check --terminal %s --run %s --peek --types question" % (coord, run)
        reply = " — reply: orca orchestration reply --id %s --body \"<text>\" --run %s --from %s" % (q["id"], run, coord)
        for text in (head + read + reply, head + reply):
            if len(text) <= HAIL_TEXT_MAX:
                return text
        return None

    def hail_question(self, sk, sid, q, run, coord):
        """(verdict, how, road) of one `hail <the skipper's session> --kind ask --when idle --no-file` (S6):
        the socket when it sits idle on this Mac, a subscription while it works, else Talk on its page
        (HAIL_SPACE, the record's `space`) — hail's own order, less the file road, which a scope skipper
        never reads. verdict None when hail could not be asked at all; the caller then cards it."""
        text = self.question_pointer(sid, q, run, coord)
        if text is None:
            return None, "the pointer is over %d characters" % HAIL_TEXT_MAX, None
        argv = [os.environ.get("WHARF_HAIL") or str(HERE / "hail"), sk["session"], "--kind", "ask", "--when", "idle",
                "--no-file", "--text", text, "--json"]
        env = dict(os.environ)
        env.pop("HAIL_SPACE", None)   # the skipper's page, never one this process was handed
        if sk.get("space"):
            env["HAIL_SPACE"] = sk["space"]
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=HAIL_TIMEOUT, env=env)
            d = json.loads(r.stdout or "{}")
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ValueError) as e:
            return None, "hail: %s" % type(e).__name__, None
        if not isinstance(d, dict) or not d.get("verdict"):
            return None, "hail exit %d: %s" % (r.returncode, ((r.stderr or "").strip().splitlines() or ["no record"])[-1][:160]), None
        return d["verdict"], "%s via %s%s" % (d["verdict"], d.get("road") or "-", (": " + str(d["why"])[:120]) if d.get("why") else ""), d.get("road")

    # -- done_when ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    def done_when(self, st):
        """(holds?, what was read) for a block Orca has completed (iac section 6's kinds)."""
        dw = st["raw"].get("done_when")
        if not dw:
            return True, "no done_when"
        (k, v), = dw.items()
        root = self.wt_of(st["id"])
        root = root if root and root.is_dir() else self.repo
        if k == "file":
            return (root / v).exists(), "file %s" % v
        if k == "marker":
            doc, _, anchor = v.partition("#")
            p = root / doc
            if not p.is_file():
                return False, "marker: %s not found" % doc
            lines = p.read_text().splitlines()
            if marker_built(lines, anchor):
                return True, "marker %s" % v
            return False, "marker %s: no \"built\" under it" % v
        if k == "check":
            if self.dry:
                return False, "check: would run `%s` (not in a dry run)" % v
            if v in self.checks:
                return self.checks[v]
            left = time_left()
            limit = 1800 if left is None else int(min(1800, left - 30))
            if limit < 30:
                return False, "check: not run, too near the tick's kill time"
            try:
                r = subprocess.run(["sh", "-c", v], cwd=str(root), capture_output=True, timeout=limit)
                got = (r.returncode == 0, "check exit %d" % r.returncode)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                got = (False, "check timed out")
            self.checks[v] = got
            return got
        if k == "memo_answered":
            memo = _mod("memo", common.tool("keel") or HERE / "keel")
            p = root / v
            if not p.is_file():
                return False, "memo %s not found" % v
            lines, found, _ = memo.parse(p.read_text())
            left = [it["id"] for it in found if not memo.yolo_settled(it, lines)]
            return not left, "memo %s%s" % (v, (": %s open" % ", ".join(left)) if left else "")
        if k == "pr_merged":
            br = self.branch(st)
            if not br:
                return False, "pr_merged: the block has no branch"
            if os.environ.get("PLAN_NO_GH"):
                return False, "pr_merged: GitHub not asked (PLAN_NO_GH)"
            if self.dry:
                return False, "pr_merged: would ask GitHub about %s (not in a dry run)" % br
            try:
                r = subprocess.run(["gh", "pr", "view", br, "--json", "state", "-q", ".state"], cwd=str(self.repo),
                                   capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
            except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
                return False, "pr %s: gh %s" % (br, type(e).__name__)
            return r.stdout.strip() == "MERGED", "pr %s %s" % (br, r.stdout.strip() or "unknown")
        return False, "done_when %s unknown" % k

    # -- one pass -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    def one_pass(self, reads, run, coord):
        """Every row of the diff acted on; the lines of what was done. Rows are read in wave order,
        so a create's deps were created earlier in the same pass."""
        bp, here = self.bp, self.here
        st_now = plan_status(self.pid)
        ended = lambda sid: (st_now.get(sid) or {}).get("status") in ENDED
        rows = blueprintlib.diff(bp, here, self.p.get("tasks") or {}, reads, answered=memo_answered(bp, self.rec, ship_mode(self.pid, bp)), ended=ended,
                                 cancelled=set(self.rec.get("respecced") or []), repo=self.repo_key)
        acted = []
        # the plan's side first: every block a plan task, with the fields Orca has no slot for
        for act, sid, detail in rows["plan"]:
            if act in ("add", "update"):
                t = self.task(sid)
                t.update(blueprintlib.plan_fields(bp, bp["by_id"][sid], here, self.repo_key))
                if t.get("seeded_branch"):
                    t["branch"] = t["seeded_branch"]
                acted.append(("plan", act, sid, detail))
            elif act == "record":
                self.task(sid)["orca_task"] = re.search(r"orca_task (\S+)", detail).group(1)
                acted.append(("plan", act, sid, detail))
        if acted and not self.dry:
            self.save()
        tasks = {t.get("id"): t for t in (reads or {}).get("tasks") or []}
        gates = {}
        for g in (reads or {}).get("gates") or []:
            gates.setdefault(g.get("task_id"), []).append(g)

        def held(st):
            # Orca makes a Task ready once its deps' Tasks complete; done_when is ours, so a dep the
            # plan has not ended (done_when unmet, or not read yet) holds the block all the same
            return [d for d in st["deps"] if (st_now.get(d) or {}).get("status") not in ENDED]

        def deps_done(tid):
            # a gated Task reads `blocked` in Orca whether or not its deps completed (P3): ask the deps
            t = tasks.get(tid) or {}
            return all(str((tasks.get(d) or {}).get("status")).lower() == "completed" for d in blueprintlib._deps_of(t))

        for act, sid, detail in rows["orca"]:
            st = bp["by_id"].get(sid) if sid else None
            tid = (self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(sid, {}).get("orca_task") if sid else None
            if act == "create":
                deps = [(self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(d, {}).get("orca_task") for d in st["deps"]]
                if not all(deps):
                    acted.append(("orca", "wait", sid, "its deps have no Task yet"))
                    continue
                if self.dry:
                    acted.append(("orca", act, sid, detail))
                    continue
                br = blueprintlib.branch_of(bp, st, here)
                res, err = self.call("task-create", sid, ["orchestration", "task-create", "--spec", blueprintlib.spec_of(bp, st),
                                                          "--task-title", sid, "--display-name", br or sid, "--run", run, "--from", coord]
                                     + (["--deps", json.dumps(deps)] if deps else []))
                new = orca()._first(res or {}, "task.id", "id")
                if err or not new:
                    acted.append(("orca", "failed", sid, "task-create: %s" % (err or json.dumps(res)[:200])))
                    continue
                self.task(sid)["orca_task"] = new
                self.save()
                tasks[new] = {"id": new, "status": orca()._first(res or {}, "task.status") or ("pending" if deps else "ready")}
                acted.append(("orca", act, sid, "task %s" % new))
            elif act == "gate":
                tid = tid or None
                if not tid:
                    acted.append(("orca", "wait", sid, "no Task to gate yet"))
                    continue
                s = st["raw"]
                if self.dry:
                    acted.append(("orca", act, sid, detail))
                    continue
                res, err = self.call("gate-create", sid, ["orchestration", "gate-create", "--task", tid, "--question",
                                                          "%s#%s" % (s["doc"], ", ".join(s["items"])), "--from", coord]
                                     + (["--options", json.dumps(s["options"])] if s.get("options") else []))
                acted.append(("orca", act if not err else "failed", sid, err or "gate %s on %s" % (orca()._first(res or {}, "gate.id", "id"), tid)))
                if not err:
                    report(self.pid, sid, "waiting", "gated on %s#%s" % (s["doc"], ", ".join(s["items"])))
            elif act == "resolve":
                pend = [g for g in gates.get(tid) or [] if str(g.get("status")).lower() == "pending"]
                text = detail.split("answered (", 1)[-1].split(") —", 1)[0]
                if not deps_done(tid) or held(st):
                    acted.append(("orca", "wait", sid, "answered; its gate resolves once %s ends" % ", ".join(held(st) or st["deps"])))
                    continue
                if self.dry or not pend:
                    acted.append(("orca", act, sid, detail))
                    continue
                _, err = self.call("gate-resolve", sid, ["orchestration", "gate-resolve", "--id", pend[0]["id"],
                                                         "--resolution", text, "--from", coord])
                if not err:
                    _, err = self.call("task-update", sid, ["orchestration", "task-update", "--id", tid, "--status", "completed",
                                                            "--result", "answered: %s" % text, "--run", run, "--from", coord])
                acted.append(("orca", act if not err else "failed", sid, err or "gate %s resolved: %s" % (pend[0]["id"], text)))
                if not err:
                    report(self.pid, sid, "done", "answered: %s" % text)
            elif act == "complete":
                if st and st["kind"] == "decision" and not deps_done(tid):
                    acted.append(("orca", "wait", sid, "resolved; completed once its deps complete"))
                    continue
                if self.dry:
                    acted.append(("orca", act, sid, detail))
                    continue
                _, err = self.call("task-update", sid, ["orchestration", "task-update", "--id", tid, "--status", "completed",
                                                        "--result", "ended in the plan", "--run", run, "--from", coord])
                acted.append(("orca", act if not err else "failed", sid, err or "task %s completed" % tid))
                if not err and st and st["kind"] == "decision" and not ended(sid):
                    # its gate was resolved without this pass (Orca's app, or a crash after gate-resolve)
                    report(self.pid, sid, "done", "gate resolved; Task %s completed" % tid)
            elif act == "start":
                if not tid:
                    acted.append(("orca", "wait", sid, "no Task yet"))
                    continue
                if held(st):
                    acted.append(("orca", "wait", sid, "ready in Orca; waits until the plan ends %s" % ", ".join(held(st))))
                    continue
                said = self.start(st, tid, run, coord)
                kind = "ok" if said.startswith("started already") else \
                       "done" if said.startswith(("built", "landed", "launched")) else \
                       "start" if said.startswith(("started", "ran", "seeded", "would", "sent")) else \
                       "raise" if said.startswith("raised") else "refuse"
                acted.append(("orca", kind, sid, said))
            elif act == "changed" and "re-spec" in detail and not self.dry:
                _, err = self.call("task-update", sid, ["orchestration", "task-update", "--id", tid, "--status", "failed",
                                                        "--result", "cancelled", "--run", run, "--from", coord])
                if not err:
                    self.task(sid).pop("orca_task", None)
                    self.rec.setdefault("respecced", []).append(tid)   # never this block's Task again (diff's cancelled)
                    self.save()
                acted.append(("orca", "re-spec" if not err else "failed", sid, err or "task %s cancelled; created again next pass" % tid))
            else:
                acted.append(("orca", act, sid, detail))
        # done_when: a block Orca completed that the plan has not ended, and one whose worker
        # reported failed — its work may be done all the same (rename S3: built and committed, its
        # suites killed for low memory): read once it reported, never rebuilt
        for st in bp["blocks"]:
            sid = st["id"]
            tid = (self.p.get("tasks") or {}).get(sid, {}).get("orca_task")
            t = tasks.get(tid) or {}
            status = str(t.get("status")).lower()
            if ended(sid):
                continue
            if status == "failed" and st["kind"] == "block" and st["raw"].get("done_when"):
                subject = worker_report(t)
                if subject is None:
                    continue
                ok, what = self.done_when(st)
                if ok:
                    if not self.dry:
                        report(self.pid, sid, "done", "built; the worker reported failed: %s" % subject)
                        self.did += ["%s: %s" % (sid, x) for x in self.release_builder(st)]
                    acted.append(("plan", "done", sid, "%s holds; the worker reported failed: %s" % (what, subject)))
                continue
            if status != "completed":
                continue
            if st["kind"] == "decision":
                # completed in Orca, not ended in the plan: the gate was resolved where this never saw it
                if not self.dry:
                    report(self.pid, sid, "done", "Orca completed its Task %s" % tid)
                acted.append(("plan", "done", sid, "Orca completed its Task"))
                continue
            ok, what = self.done_when(st)
            last = (st_now.get(sid) or {}).get("progress")
            if ok:
                if not self.dry:
                    report(self.pid, sid, "done", "Orca completed it; %s" % what)
                    self.did += ["%s: %s" % (sid, x) for x in self.release_builder(st)]
                acted.append(("plan", "done", sid, what))
            elif last != "done_when not met: %s" % what:
                if not self.dry:
                    report(self.pid, sid, "blocked", "done_when not met: %s" % what)
                acted.append(("plan", "unmet", sid, what))
        acted += self.relay_questions(run, coord)
        return acted

    def apply(self, once):
        """Passes until one acts on nothing, at most PASSES; --once is one."""
        lost = [] if self.dry else self.dangling()
        for e in lost:
            self.did.append("ledger: %s %s was sent and never recorded — Orca's state decides" % (e["op"], e.get("block") or ""))
        run, coord = (self.rec.get("orca_run"), self.rec.get("coordinator")) if self.dry else self.ensure_run()
        for e in lost:
            # after ensure_run: the coordinator the crash left may be gone; a failed update here is
            # sent again by start(), which finds the `unknown` shell line while Orca still says ready
            if e["op"] == "shell" and e.get("task"):
                self.call("task-update", e["block"], ["orchestration", "task-update", "--id", e["task"], "--status", "failed",
                                                      "--result", "interrupted: the command's result was never recorded",
                                                      "--run", run, "--from", coord])
                report(self.pid, e["block"], "failed", "interrupted shell block: not run again blindly")
        lines = []
        for n in range(1 if once else PASSES):
            _cache.pop("fetched", None)   # a pinned ship's decision docs: fetched at most once a pass
            _cache.pop("onmain", None)    # origin/<main>: fetched at most once a pass (on_main)
            _cache.pop("onmain_own", None)   # a ship's own commits (own_commit_ids), read again each pass
            reads = None
            if run:
                reads, why = orca_reads(run, coord)
                if why:
                    raise Refused("Orca unread — %s" % why, 3)
            acted = self.one_pass(reads, run, coord)
            real = [x for x in acted if x[1] not in ("ok", "wait", "stalled", "failed", "orphan", "refuse", "raise", "changed")]
            lines.append((n + 1, acted))
            if self.dry or not real:
                break
        if not self.dry and run:
            self.finish_if_ended()
        return lines

    def finish_if_ended(self):
        """Every block ended in the plan: the ship is marked ended (the tick stops visiting it) and its
        coordinator terminal closed, so a finished ship leaves no tab in Orca. The Run stays: Orca has
        no run delete, and its history is the record."""
        st = plan_status(self.pid)
        if self.rec.get("ended") or not all((st.get(s["id"]) or {}).get("status") in ENDED for s in self.bp["blocks"]):
            return
        self.rec["ended"] = helmlib.now()
        coord = self.rec.get("coordinator")
        if coord:
            _, err = orca()._call(None, ["terminal", "close", "--terminal", coord, "--tab"], timeout=60)
            self.rec["coordinator_closed"] = not err
        self.save()
        self.did.append("every block ended: the ship is marked ended%s" % (", its coordinator %s closed" % coord if coord and self.rec["coordinator_closed"] else ""))


def brake_refusal():
    """Why a start waits for the studio brake, or None (S1 of the skipper-resilience build): the file
    `~/.studio-brake` (the studio brake, a script outside this module: music is on and the agent host
    steps aside), or — with `wharf-runs/brake-label` naming the launchd job the brake stops — that job's
    process in state `T`, stopped. The probe's start ran under the file untouched: nothing in wharf
    read it. wharf only reads the brake, and it holds new starts only: a worker already running is braked by
    no one."""
    home = Path(os.environ.get("HOME") or Path.home())
    if (home / ".studio-brake").exists():
        return "%s exists" % (home / ".studio-brake")
    label = common.config_line("wharf-runs/brake-label")
    if not label:
        return None
    try:
        out = subprocess.run([os.environ.get("WHARF_LAUNCHCTL") or "launchctl", "list", label],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20).stdout
        m = re.search(r'"PID"\s*=\s*(\d+);', out)
        if not m:
            return None
        stat = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "stat=", "-p", m.group(1)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20).stdout.strip()
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    return "%s (pid %s) is stopped" % (label, m.group(1)) if stat.startswith("T") else None


class Refused(Exception):
    def __init__(self, msg, code=2):
        Exception.__init__(self, msg)
        self.code = code


def _git(cwd, *argv):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(cwd)] + list(argv), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    return r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else None


def lock(pid, ship):
    """The strict lock: one apply per ship at a time (the tick's and an attended one)."""
    d = helmlib.plan_dir(pid)
    f = open(str(d / ("wharf-%s.lock" % ship)), "w")
    try:
        fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        f.close()
        return None
    return f


def say_once(pid, ship, quiet, text, dry=False):
    """A ship's refusal line: said always when attended; in the tick (quiet) only when it differs
    from what the last tick said for this ship (the .said file the standing rows use too)."""
    if not quiet:
        say(text)
        return
    said = helmlib.plan_dir(pid) / ("wharf-%s.said" % ship)
    try:
        before = said.read_text()
    except OSError:
        before = None
    if before != text:
        say(text)
        try:
            said.write_text(text)   # a dry tick's one write, as for the standing rows
        except OSError:
            pass


def apply_ship(pid, path, dry=False, once=False, as_json=False, quiet=False, launch=None):
    """One ship: the digest, the lock, the passes. Returns the exit code."""
    bp = load_blueprint(path, pid)
    ship = Ship(pid, bp, dry, launch)
    d, sd = blueprintlib.digest(bp), blueprintlib.block_digests(bp)
    rec = ship.rec
    if rec.get("pin") and rec.get("file") and os.path.realpath(path) != os.path.realpath(rec["file"]):
        # a pinned ship is keyed on its pin: its text is the plan's copy, never a checkout's file,
        # which may be a later push the yard never fetched
        say_once(pid, bp["name"], quiet, "wharf apply: %s refused — it is pinned (%s): its blueprint is %s, and "
                 "`wharf apply --yard` rejoins it" % (bp["name"], pin_label(rec["pin"]), rec["file"]), dry)
        return 2
    if rec.get("digest") and rec["digest"] != d:
        say_once(pid, bp["name"], quiet, "wharf apply: %s refused — %s; `wharf check %s --plan %s --accept` re-records it, then a "
                 "pending Task is re-specced and a dispatched one becomes a card (Q1)" % (bp["name"], change_text(rec, d, sd), path, pid), dry)
        return 1
    if dry and not rec.get("orca_run"):
        return dry_run(pid, path)
    if once and rec.get("ended"):
        if not quiet:
            say("wharf apply --once: %s ended %s — an attended `wharf apply` opens it again" % (bp["name"], helmlib.iso(rec["ended"])[:16]))
        return 0
    if once and not rec.get("orca_run"):
        say("wharf apply --once: %s has no Run — its first compile is an attended `wharf apply`" % bp["name"])
        return 2
    held = None if dry else lock(pid, bp["name"])
    if not dry and held is None:
        say("wharf apply: %s is being applied by another run (its lock in %s)" % (bp["name"], helmlib.plan_dir(pid)))
        return 4
    try:
        if not dry:
            ship.reload()   # under the lock: what was read before it may be another apply's past
            rec = ship.rec
        clash = ship.clash()
        if clash:
            say_once(pid, bp["name"], quiet, "wharf apply: %s refused — block ids already another ship's plan task in plan %s: %s (rename them)"
                     % (bp["name"], pid, ", ".join(clash)))
            return 2
        if not dry and not orca()._app_up():
            say_once(pid, bp["name"], quiet, "wharf apply: Orca is not running here (open the app; a session in VS Code clears ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE)", dry)
            return 3
        warned = "; ".join(bp.get("yard_warnings") or [])
        if warned and not dry and rec.get("yard_warned") != warned:
            # a ship laid before its scope had a yard keeps going; its far block is said once, here
            # and in the tick's log, and a new compile of the same text is refused (blueprintlib.load)
            say("wharf apply: %s: warning — %s (laid before its scope had a yard: it goes on, a new compile is refused)"
                % (bp["name"], warned))
            rec["yard_warned"] = warned
            ship.save()
        if rec.get("ended") and not dry:
            rec.pop("ended", None)   # applied again: open, until every block has ended once more
        if not rec.get("digest") and not dry:
            accept(rec, path, d, sd)
            ship.did.append("digest %s recorded (the first apply)" % d[:12])
        if not dry and bp["meta"].get("mode") and "mode" not in ship.p and not ship.p.get("mode_refused"):
            # the blueprint's mode, once (skipper-modes S1): plan.json holds it from here, and `helm
            # mode` rewrites it there — a later apply never puts the file's word back over the owner's.
            # An unattended or --once apply never records a raise (S3b), and its refusal is kept in
            # plan.json: the next tick's apply, from launchd with no CLAUDE_UNATTENDED, would otherwise
            # record the run-written mode (landing review 9)
            why, torn = bp_mode_judge(pid, bp, once)
            if why and torn:
                ship.did.append("mode %s not recorded now: repos.json is unreadable, so the ship reads ask, and a "
                                "refusal against that is kept nowhere — the next apply judges it again" % bp["meta"]["mode"])
            elif why:
                ship.p["mode_refused"] = ship.refused_now = {"mode": bp["meta"]["mode"], "why": why, "ts": helmlib.now()}
                ship.save()
                ship.did.append("mode %s not recorded, and never by a later apply (`helm mode %s %s` records it): %s"
                                % (bp["meta"]["mode"], pid, bp["meta"]["mode"], why))
            else:
                ship.p["mode"] = bp["meta"]["mode"]
                ship.save()
                ship.did.append("mode %s recorded (the blueprint's)" % bp["meta"]["mode"])
        elif not once and refused_line(pid, bp, ship.p):
            ship.did.append(refused_line(pid, bp, ship.p))
        if not dry and not ship.p.get("started"):
            # the ship's start, once (H1), here and not in the digest branch: a blueprint accepted
            # first with `wharf check --accept` has its digest already. A ship applied before rename
            # S5 has none, and its card reads its first running task instead (helmlib.state)
            ship.p["started"] = helmlib.now()
            ship.save()
        try:
            passes = ship.apply(once)
        except Refused as e:
            say_once(pid, bp["name"], quiet and not ship.did, "\n".join(["wharf apply: %s — %s" % (bp["name"], e)]
                                                                       + ["  %s" % x for x in ship.did]), dry)
            return e.code
    finally:
        if held:
            held.close()
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"ship": bp["name"], "plan": pid, "run": ship.rec.get("orca_run"), "coordinator": ship.rec.get("coordinator"),
                          "did": ship.did, "passes": [{"pass": n, "rows": [list(r) for r in rows]} for n, rows in passes]},
                         ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True))
        return 0
    # quiet (the tick's): print a ship that acted, or whose standing rows (a refusal, a failure, a
    # card) differ from what the last tick said — a ship that only waits is said once, not every 5 min
    busy = any(r[1] not in ("ok", "wait", "refuse", "raise", "changed", "orphan", "failed") and not str(r[3]).startswith("would")
               for _, rows in passes for r in rows) or ship.did
    standing = sorted(set("%s %s %s" % (r[1], r[2], r[3]) for _, rows in passes for r in rows
                          if r[1] in ("refuse", "raise", "changed", "orphan", "failed")))
    said = helmlib.plan_dir(pid) / ("wharf-%s.said" % bp["name"])
    try:
        before = said.read_text()
    except OSError:
        before = None
    now_said = "\n".join(standing)
    if quiet and standing and before != now_said:
        busy = True
    if quiet:   # a dry tick too: the disarmed tick is dry every 5 min, and this note is its only write
        try:
            said.write_text(now_said)
        except OSError:
            pass
    if quiet and not busy:
        return 0
    say("wharf apply%s: %s — plan %s, Run %s (coordinator %s)" % (" --once" if once else " --dry-run" if dry else "", bp["name"], pid,
                                                                 ship.rec.get("orca_run") or "—", ship.rec.get("coordinator") or "—"))
    for x in ship.did:
        say("  %s" % x)
    width = max([len(s["id"]) for s in bp["blocks"]] + [1])
    for n, rows in passes:
        if len(passes) > 1:
            say(" pass %d" % n)
        for side, act, sid, detail in rows:
            if quiet and act == "ok":
                continue
            say("  %-5s %-8s %-*s  %s" % (side, act, width, sid or "—", detail))
    return 0


def refused_line(pid, bp, p):
    """A blueprint mode an unattended apply refused (plan.json's `mode_refused`), said again to a person's
    apply with the line that lifts it, or None: it was said once, to a run nobody watched, and stood
    silent after (follow-ups item 3). Not once the ship has a mode: `helm mode` spoke, and drops it."""
    r = p.get("mode_refused")
    m = isinstance(r, dict) and (r.get("mode") or bp["meta"].get("mode"))
    if not m or "mode" in p or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"):
        return None
    return "mode %s refused %s, and not recorded since (`helm mode %s %s` records it): %s" % (
        m, helmlib.iso(r.get("ts")) or "earlier", pid, m, r.get("why") or "a raise by an unattended apply")


def dry_run(pid, path, as_json=False):
    """B6's dry run (`plan apply --dry-run`): the diff against Orca and the plan, nothing written."""
    bp = load_blueprint(path, pid)
    here = helmlib.host()
    p = need(pid)
    rec = (p.get("blueprints") or {}).get(bp["name"]) or {}
    d, sd = blueprintlib.digest(bp), blueprintlib.block_digests(bp)
    refused = bool(rec.get("digest")) and rec["digest"] != d
    reads = None
    if rec.get("orca_run"):
        reads, why = orca_reads(rec["orca_run"], rec.get("coordinator"))
        if why:
            print("wharf apply: Orca unread — %s; with Run %s recorded, a diff without it would be wrong" % (why, rec["orca_run"]),
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
    st = plan_status(pid)
    ended = lambda sid: (st.get(sid) or {}).get("status") in ENDED
    rows = blueprintlib.diff(bp, here, p.get("tasks") or {}, reads, answered=memo_answered(bp, rec, ship_mode(pid, bp)), ended=ended,
                             cancelled=set(rec.get("respecced") or []), repo=ship_repo(bp, rec)[0])
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"ship": bp["name"], "file": bp["path"], "plan": pid, "digest": d, "accepted": rec.get("digest"),
                          "refused": refused, "orca_run": rec.get("orca_run"),
                          "rows": {k: [list(r) for r in v] for k, v in rows.items()}}, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True))
        return 1 if refused else 0
    say("wharf apply --dry-run: %s (%s) against plan %s — nothing is called that writes" % (bp["name"], path, pid))
    if rec.get("digest"):
        say("digest %s: %s" % (d[:12], change_text(rec, d, sd)))
    else:
        say("digest %s: not recorded — the first apply records it (wharf check --accept records it now)" % d[:12])
    if refused_line(pid, bp, p):
        say(refused_line(pid, bp, p))
    if reads is None:
        say("orca: no Run recorded for this blueprint — run-create \"%s/%s (wharf apply)\" first; nothing to read" % (bp["meta"]["repo"], bp["name"]))
    else:
        r = reads["run"] or {}
        say("orca: Run %s (coordinator %s): %d tasks, %d gates, %d dispatches" % (
            r.get("id") or rec["orca_run"], r.get("coordinator_handle") or "?", len(reads["tasks"]), len(reads["gates"]), len(reads["workers"])))
    width = max([len(s["id"]) for s in bp["blocks"]] + [1])
    for side in ("orca", "plan"):
        say("%s:" % side)
        for act, sid, detail in rows[side]:
            say("  %-8s %-*s  %s" % (act, width, sid or "—", detail))
    counts = {}
    for act, _, _ in rows["orca"] + rows["plan"]:
        if act != "ok":
            counts[act] = counts.get(act, 0) + 1
    say("to do: %s" % (", ".join("%d %s" % (n, k) for k, n in sorted(counts.items())) or "nothing — Orca and the plan match the file"))
    if refused:
        say("wharf apply: refused — %s; `wharf check %s --accept` re-records it, then a pending Task is re-specced "
            "and a dispatched one becomes a card (Q1)" % (change_text(rec, d, sd), path))
        return 1
    return 0


def ships_with_runs():
    """[(plan id, blueprint file, ship, None or a plan)] of every ship on this Mac with a Run recorded.
    A pinned ship (wharf apply --yard) is keyed on its pin, its file the plan's copy: a second un-ended
    record of one pin — two plans compiled one blueprint and both drove before the refusal existed
    (31157269, 2230a94e) — carries the plan id of the one accepted first in the last place, and the
    tick drives that one only."""
    rows, first = [], {}
    for pid in helmlib.list_plans():
        p = helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}
        for name, rec in sorted((p.get("blueprints") or {}).items()):
            if rec.get("orca_run") and rec.get("file") and not rec.get("ended"):
                k = pin_key(rec.get("pin"))
                rows.append((pid, blueprint_file(rec) or rec["file"], name, k))
                at = (rec.get("accepted") or 0, pid)
                if k and (k not in first or at < first[k]):
                    first[k] = at
    return [(pid, f, name, first[k][1] if k and first[k][1] != pid else None, bool(k)) for pid, f, name, k in rows]


def tick_fence(f, pid):
    """Why the tick leaves an unpinned ship alone on this Mac, or None: its scope gained a yard that is
    another host (a plain apply made before the overlay named one), so the yard drives it, not two Macs.
    A registry that does not read fails closed, as yard_fence does."""
    if common.registry_unreadable():
        return "the registry %s does not read, so which host drives it cannot be told" % common.repos_json()
    _, scope, yard = blueprintlib.scope_yard_of(load_blueprint(f, pid)["meta"]["repo"])
    if yard and yard != harness().machine():
        return "its scope %s drives on %s — not driven here (lay it there with --yard)" % (scope, yard)
    return None


def tick_caller(environ=None):
    """None when this process is the yard's tick — launchd's `ask poll` running `helm tick`, or the
    owner's own shell — else what it is instead. Only the tick's --once --all hands a ship its launch
    (S6), because the launch carries the keel's yes to merge (`--by ship`) and a flag that stands for a
    person's yes refuses an unattended caller (AGENTS.md's trap): a session (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), a
    dispatched run (CLAUDE_UNATTENDED, DISPATCH_DEPTH past 0), a skipper (SKIPPER_SCOPE) or a ship's
    block (its env, helmlib.ENV_NAMES) running `wharf apply --once --all` gets today's raise instead.
    autofinish-run checks the same names again (its ship_caller_refusal): this only keeps the pass
    from asking for what would be refused."""
    env = os.environ if environ is None else environ
    for n in ("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID", "CLAUDE_UNATTENDED", "SKIPPER_SCOPE") + tuple(helmlib.ENV_NAMES["ship"]):
        if env.get(n):
            return "%s is set" % n
    if (env.get("DISPATCH_DEPTH") or "0").strip() != "0":
        return "DISPATCH_DEPTH=%s" % env["DISPATCH_DEPTH"]
    return None


def ship_scope(bp=None, rec=None):
    """(scope, yard) of a ship: its pin's registry key when pinned (the yard never resolves a caller's
    path), else its blueprint's repo; (None, None) when the registry does not say."""
    pin = (rec or {}).get("pin")
    if isinstance(pin, dict) and pin.get("repo"):
        scope = common.scope_of_key(pin["repo"])
        return scope, (common.scope_yard(scope) if scope else None)
    if bp is None:
        return None, None
    _, scope, yard = blueprintlib.scope_yard_of(bp["meta"]["repo"])
    return scope, yard


def yard_launch(pid, name, path):
    """The launch dict the tick's pass hands ship NAME of plan PID (S6, the yard component's "The
    `--once --all` pass launches"): --watch's default of 2 launches at once, no session (the tick has
    none), and `yard` naming the scope, which start_launch reads to add the landing call
    (Ship.merge_flags). None off the ship's yard, so its `launch: finish` block is raised as before; a
    registry that does not read is None too: which host is the yard cannot be told."""
    if common.registry_unreadable():
        return None
    rec = ((helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}).get("blueprints") or {}).get(name) or {}
    scope, yard = ship_scope(None if isinstance(rec.get("pin"), dict) else load_blueprint(path, pid), rec)
    if not yard or yard != harness().machine():
        return None
    return {"launches": 2, "session": None, "yard": scope}


def cmd_apply(a):
    if (a.no_merge or a.gen is not None) and not a.yard:
        raise SystemExit("wharf apply: --no-merge and --gen go with --yard")
    if (a.pinned or a.laid_by) and not a.yard:
        raise SystemExit("wharf apply: --pinned and --laid-by are --yard's, the yard's side over ssh")
    if a.yard:
        return cmd_yard(a)
    if a.all:
        if not a.once:
            raise SystemExit("wharf apply --all is the tick's: --once with it")
        rc = 0
        _cache["tick"] = 0   # session starts this tick, every ship together (TICK_STARTS)
        # S6: only the tick itself launches, and only on a ship's own yard (yard_launch)
        tick = tick_caller() is None
        for pid, f, name, held, pinned in ships_with_runs():
            if held:
                say_once(pid, name, True, "wharf apply --once: plan %s's %s is a pin plan %s drives already — not driven twice "
                         "(end one of them)" % (pid, name, held), a.dry_run)
                continue
            if not Path(f).is_file():
                say_once(pid, name, True, "wharf apply --once: plan %s's blueprint %s is gone from this Mac" % (pid, f), a.dry_run)
                continue
            # one ship's bad file or crash is its own line; the ships after it are still visited
            try:
                why = None if pinned else tick_fence(f, pid)
                if why:
                    say_once(pid, name, True, "wharf apply --once: plan %s's %s: %s" % (pid, name, why), a.dry_run)
                    continue
                launch = yard_launch(pid, name, f) if tick else None
                rc = max(rc, apply_ship(pid, f, dry=a.dry_run, once=True, quiet=True, launch=launch))
            except SystemExit as e:
                say_once(pid, name, True, "wharf apply --once: %s (plan %s): exit %s" % (f, pid, e.code if isinstance(e.code, int) else e.code or ""))
                rc = max(rc, e.code if isinstance(e.code, int) else 2)
            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
                say_once(pid, name, True, "wharf apply --once: %s (plan %s): %s: %s" % (f, pid, type(e).__name__, str(e)[:200]))
                rc = max(rc, 2)
        return rc
    if a.watch:
        return cmd_watch(a)
    if len(a.files) != 1:
        raise SystemExit("wharf apply: one blueprint file (several with --watch), or --once --all")
    a.file = a.files[0]
    if not a.dry_run:
        why = yard_fence(load_blueprint(a.file, a.plan))
        if why:
            print("wharf apply: refused: %s" % why, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    pid = plan_id(a.plan)
    launch = None
    if a.launch:
        if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"):
            raise SystemExit("wharf apply --launch: a launch starts from an attended apply only (CLAUDE_UNATTENDED=%s)"
                             % os.environ["CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"])
        launch = {"launches": a.launches, "session": a.session or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID")}
    if a.dry_run and not a.once:
        return dry_run(pid, a.file, a.json)
    return apply_ship(pid, a.file, dry=a.dry_run, once=a.once, as_json=a.json, quiet=a.quiet, launch=launch)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- the yard (skipper-resilience S2)

YARD_ONLY = "the yard's flags come over ssh from a caller, never from a session here"
DIGEST_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$")


def yard_fence(bp):
    """Why a plain `wharf apply` of BP is refused on this host, or None: the yard's fence, one driver
    per ship (the proposal's yard component). A ship whose repo's scope has a yard is laid there with
    --yard and driven there by the tick; a scope with no yard — absent or null, every scope until the
    overlay names them (S3) — is refused nothing. A registry that does not read fails closed (the
    torn-registry trap): which host drives cannot be told."""
    if common.registry_unreadable():
        return "the registry %s does not read, so whether %s's scope has a yard cannot be told" % (common.repos_json(), bp["meta"]["repo"])
    _, scope, yard = blueprintlib.scope_yard_of(bp["meta"]["repo"])
    if not yard:
        return None
    if yard != harness().machine():
        return "%s's scope %s drives on %s; lay it with --yard" % (bp["meta"]["repo"], scope, yard)
    return "on the yard a ship is laid with --yard (or --once --all, the tick's)"


def yard_scope(bp):
    """(registry key, scope, yard) of BP's repo, or Refused: --yard lays only a ship whose scope has a yard."""
    if common.registry_unreadable():
        raise Refused("the registry %s does not read: no scope's yard can be told" % common.repos_json())
    key, scope, yard = blueprintlib.scope_yard_of(bp["meta"]["repo"])
    if not scope:
        raise Refused("%s is in no scope (scopes check)" % bp["meta"]["repo"])
    if not yard:
        raise Refused("scope %s has no yard (scopes set %s --yard HOST names one)" % (scope, scope))
    return key, scope, yard


def pin_scope(pin):
    """(scope, yard) of a pin's repo, its registry key as the caller resolved it, or Refused as yard_scope."""
    if common.registry_unreadable():
        raise Refused("the registry %s does not read: no scope's yard can be told" % common.repos_json())
    scope = common.scope_of_key(pin["repo"])
    if not scope:
        raise Refused("%s is in no scope here (scopes check)" % pin["repo"])
    yard = common.scope_yard(scope)
    if not yard:
        raise Refused("scope %s has no yard (scopes set %s --yard HOST names one)" % (scope, scope))
    return scope, yard


def pin_key(pin):
    """What a pin is, its digest aside: the same file on the same branch is the same ship, pushed again or not."""
    return (pin.get("repo"), pin.get("branch"), pin.get("rel")) if isinstance(pin, dict) else None


def pin_label(pin):
    return "%s %s:%s" % (pin.get("repo"), pin.get("branch"), pin.get("rel"))


def pinned_by(pin, other_than=None):
    """(plan id, ship) of an un-ended ship on this Mac pinned to PIN in a plan other than OTHER_THAN, or None."""
    for pid in helmlib.list_plans():
        if pid == other_than:
            continue
        for name, rec in sorted(((helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}).get("blueprints") or {}).items()):
            if not rec.get("ended") and pin_key(rec.get("pin")) == pin_key(pin):
                return pid, name
    return None


def laid_by_here():
    """Who lays the ship, read on the calling Mac — never on the yard, where ssh has carried no
    environment: unattended when CLAUDE_UNATTENDED is set, DISPATCH_DEPTH is not 0, or a ship's env is."""
    raw = os.environ.get("DISPATCH_DEPTH") or "0"
    # a ship's block (a shell command, an Orca worker) carries the ship's env (helmlib's ENV_NAMES)
    # and no CLAUDE_UNATTENDED: no person laid it, and S6 reads `attended` as a person's yes to merge
    unattended = (bool(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED")) or raw != "0"
                  or any(os.environ.get(n) for n in helmlib.ENV_NAMES["ship"]))
    return {"mode": "unattended" if unattended else "attended", "depth": int(raw) if raw.isdigit() else 0,
            "session": os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID"), "host": harness().machine(), "t": helmlib.now()}


def merge_value(bp, no_merge, laid_by):
    """The merge the launch asks for, decided at the keel and kept as data (S6's start_launch reads it):
    merge unless --no-merge (the keel), the blueprint's `merge: no` or an unattended layer says no."""
    said = blueprintlib.merge_of(bp["meta"])
    if no_merge:
        return {"value": "no", "why": "keel"}
    if said == "no":
        return {"value": "no", "why": "blueprint"}
    if laid_by.get("mode") == "unattended":
        return {"value": "no", "why": "unattended"}
    return {"value": "yes", "why": "blueprint" if said == "yes" else "default"}


def _git_text(cwd, *argv):
    """git's stdout as it is (a file's text, unstripped), or None."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(cwd)] + list(argv), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    return r.stdout if r.returncode == 0 else None


def yard_alias(yard):
    """How this Mac reaches YARD over ssh: `wharf-runs/ssh`'s `<host>:<alias>` line (orca-host --on's
    key), else bin/harness's peers; None when neither names it."""
    for line in common.config_lines("wharf-runs/ssh") or []:
        host, _, alias = line.partition(":")
        if host.strip().lower() == yard.lower() and alias.strip():
            return alias.strip()
    return harness().peers().get(yard)


# The caller's side over ssh, read by `sh -s -- <flags>` on the yard: the yard's own wharf, found by the
# yard's own config — the core's module in the checkout its `home` names (the overlay's shim came first
# until B14b, 2026-10-23, which deleted it). ssh carries no environment, so nothing here is the caller's
# but the flags.
REMOTE_WHARF = r'''set -u
c=${REGATTA_CONFIG:-$HOME/.config/regatta}
w=
h=$(head -n 1 "$c/home" 2>/dev/null)
case $h in "~"*) h=$HOME${h#"~"};; esac
if [ -n "$h" ] && [ -x "$h/modules/wharf-runs/bin/wharf" ]; then w=$h/modules/wharf-runs/bin/wharf; fi
[ -n "$w" ] || { echo "no wharf on $(hostname -s): no core's module ($c)" >&2; exit 2; }
PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH
export PATH
exec "$w" apply --yard "$@" </dev/null
'''


def cmd_yard(a):
    """`wharf apply --yard`: the caller's side (a blueprint file), or the yard's (--pinned, --laid-by)."""
    if a.all or a.once or a.watch or a.dry_run or a.launch:
        raise SystemExit("wharf apply --yard: lays one ship on its yard; not with --all, --once, --watch, --dry-run or --launch")
    try:
        if a.pinned or a.laid_by:
            if not (a.pinned and a.laid_by) or a.files:
                raise Refused("--pinned and --laid-by come together and with no file: the caller's ssh sends them")
            return yard_side(a)
        if len(a.files) != 1:
            raise Refused("one blueprint file")
        return yard_caller(a)
    except Refused as e:
        print("wharf apply --yard: refused: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        return e.code


def yard_caller(a):
    """The blueprint as committed and pushed: pinned, its scope's yard found, then compiled here when
    this is the yard, else over the yard's ssh alias. Exit: the compile's."""
    f = Path(a.files[0]).resolve()
    if not f.is_file():
        raise Refused("%s: no such file" % a.files[0])
    top = _git(f.parent, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")
    if not top:
        raise Refused("%s is in no git checkout: the yard reads a blueprint from origin" % f)
    branch = _git(top, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "HEAD")
    if not branch or branch == "HEAD":
        raise Refused("%s is on no branch (a detached HEAD): the yard reads origin/<branch>" % top)
    rel = _git(f.parent, "ls-files", "--full-name", "--", f.name)
    if not rel:
        raise Refused("%s is not committed: commit it, then push it — the yard reads origin/%s:<its path>" % (f, branch))
    # the yard reads origin's text, so the caller's must be that text: pushed, and nothing changed since
    if _git_text(top, "show", "origin/%s:%s" % (branch, rel)) != f.read_text():
        raise Refused("push it first: the yard reads origin/%s:%s" % (branch, rel))
    bp = load_blueprint(str(f))
    key, scope, yard = yard_scope(bp)
    # judged as the yard will load it (key=, that repo's own hosts), not by a path `repo:`'s union of
    # every repo's hosts: else a `host:` passes here and the lay is refused only after the ssh
    try:
        blueprintlib.load(str(f), key=key)
    except blueprintlib.BlueprintError as e:
        raise Refused("as the yard reads it (repo %s): %s" % (key, "; ".join(e.problems)))
    pin = {"repo": key, "branch": branch, "rel": rel, "digest": blueprintlib.digest(bp)}
    laid = laid_by_here()
    pid = plan_id(a.plan)
    if yard == harness().machine():
        return yard_compile(pin, laid, pid, a)
    depth_refusal(laid)   # said here, before the ssh: the yard would refuse it as well
    alias = yard_alias(yard)
    if not alias:
        raise Refused("scope %s's yard %s has no ssh alias here (wharf-runs/ssh: %s:<alias>)" % (scope, yard, yard))
    # ssh carries no environment: the caller's SKIPPER_GEN goes across as --gen
    gen = a.gen if a.gen is not None else (os.environ.get("SKIPPER_GEN") or "").strip() or None
    flags = (["--pinned", json.dumps(pin, sort_keys=True), "--laid-by", json.dumps(laid, sort_keys=True), "--plan", pid]
             + (["--no-merge"] if a.no_merge else []) + (["--gen", str(gen)] if gen is not None else [])
             + (["--json"] if a.json else []))
    argv = [os.environ.get("WHARF_SSH") or harness().SSH, "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=10", alias,
            "sh -s -- " + " ".join(shlex.quote(x) for x in flags)]
    if not a.json:
        say("wharf apply --yard: %s pinned at %s; laying it on %s (%s)" % (pin_label(pin), pin["digest"][:12], yard, alias))
    raw = os.environ.get("WHARF_YARD_TIMEOUT") or "1200"
    if not raw.isdigit():
        raise Refused("WHARF_YARD_TIMEOUT=%s is not a number" % raw[:40])
    ceiling = int(raw)
    try:
        # its output relayed as it comes, its exit kept; a ceiling well past a lay's git fetch (120 s)
        # and its Orca calls, so a yard that hangs after connecting never holds the caller for good
        r = subprocess.run(argv, input=REMOTE_WHARF, text=True, timeout=ceiling)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise Refused("ssh %s: no answer from the yard in %ss (WHARF_YARD_TIMEOUT); the lay may have gone through: "
                      "`wharf status` on the yard before laying it again" % (alias, ceiling), 1)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refused("ssh %s: %s" % (alias, e), 1)
    if r.returncode == 255:
        print("wharf apply --yard: ssh %s exit 255 — the yard was not reached, or ssh itself failed" % alias, file=sys.stderr)
    return r.returncode


def depth_refusal(laid):
    raw = os.environ.get("DISPATCH_MAX_DEPTH") or "5"   # bin/dispatch's maxdepth, the same default
    if not raw.isdigit():
        raise Refused("DISPATCH_MAX_DEPTH=%s is not a number" % raw[:40])
    most = int(raw)
    if laid["depth"] > most:
        raise Refused("laid_by.depth %d is past dispatch's cap (DISPATCH_MAX_DEPTH %d): past it a person lays the next"
                      % (laid["depth"], most))


def yard_side(a):
    """The yard's side of --yard, as the caller's ssh runs it: the pin and laid_by as the caller sent
    them, never read from a session here."""
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID") or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"):
        raise Refused(YARD_ONLY)
    try:
        pin, laid = json.loads(a.pinned), json.loads(a.laid_by)
    except ValueError:
        raise Refused("--pinned and --laid-by are JSON objects")
    if not (isinstance(pin, dict) and all(isinstance(pin.get(k), str) and pin[k] for k in ("repo", "branch", "rel"))
            and DIGEST_RE.match(str(pin.get("digest") or ""))):
        raise Refused("--pinned is {repo, branch, rel, digest}: %s" % a.pinned[:200])
    if not (isinstance(laid, dict) and laid.get("mode") in ("attended", "unattended")
            and isinstance(laid.get("depth"), int) and not isinstance(laid.get("depth"), bool) and laid["depth"] >= 0):
        raise Refused("--laid-by is {mode: attended|unattended, depth, session, host, t}: %s" % a.laid_by[:200])
    if pin["branch"].startswith("-") or pin["rel"].startswith("-"):
        raise Refused("--pinned's branch and rel never start with '-' (git would read an option): %s" % a.pinned[:200])
    if not a.plan:
        raise Refused("--pinned comes with --plan: the caller names the plan")
    try:
        helmlib.plan_dir(a.plan)
    except ValueError as e:
        raise Refused("--plan %s: %s" % (a.plan[:80], e))
    # ssh sends no environment: the caller's layer is restored here, so start_refusal judges a lay
    # through the yard exactly as one made on it (an unattended or nested layer starts no session)
    if laid["mode"] == "unattended":
        os.environ["CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"] = "laid_by"
    os.environ["DISPATCH_DEPTH"] = str(laid["depth"])
    return yard_compile(pin, laid, a.plan, a)


def yard_lock():
    """One --yard compile at a time on this Mac: the pin's refusal reads every plan, then records."""
    root = helmlib.plans_root()
    root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    f = open(str(root / ".wharf-yard.lock"), "w")
    fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
    return f


def yard_compile(pin, laid, pid, a):
    """On the yard: the pin read from origin, checked, kept in the plan, then the first apply."""
    here = harness().machine()
    depth_refusal(laid)
    main = repo_path(pin["repo"])
    if not (main / ".git").exists():
        raise Refused("%s is not cloned on %s (repos --clone there)" % (pin["repo"], here))
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(main), "fetch", "-q", "origin", pin["branch"]], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
        fetched = r.returncode == 0
        why = (r.stderr or "").strip()[-200:]
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        fetched, why = False, str(e)
    if not fetched:
        raise Refused("git fetch origin %s in %s: %s" % (pin["branch"], main, why or "failed"), 1)
    text = _git_text(main, "show", "origin/%s:%s" % (pin["branch"], pin["rel"]))
    if text is None:
        raise Refused("origin/%s:%s is not there as %s fetched it" % (pin["branch"], pin["rel"], here))
    # the pin's repo is the key here, never the blueprint's `repo:` (a caller's path means nothing on
    # this Mac); a ship this plan already accepted is read as in flight (load's yard_warnings)
    accepted = set(r["digest"] for r in ((helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}).get("blueprints") or {}).values()
                   if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get("digest"))
    try:
        bp = blueprintlib.load(main / pin["rel"], text=text, key=pin["repo"], accepted=accepted)
    except blueprintlib.BlueprintError as e:
        print("wharf: origin/%s:%s is not a valid blueprint:" % (pin["branch"], pin["rel"]), file=sys.stderr)
        for x in e.problems:
            print("  - %s" % x, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    d = blueprintlib.digest(bp)
    if d != pin["digest"]:
        raise Refused("origin/%s:%s reads digest %s here, not the pinned %s: pushed again since — lay it again"
                      % (pin["branch"], pin["rel"], d[:12], pin["digest"][:12]))
    scope, yard = pin_scope(pin)
    key = pin["repo"]
    if yard != here:
        raise Refused("%s is not scope %s's yard (%s): it lays the ship there" % (here, scope, yard))
    lease = yard_lease()
    name = bp["name"]
    merge = merge_value(bp, a.no_merge, laid)
    held = yard_lock()
    try:
        other = pinned_by(pin, other_than=pid)
        if other:
            raise Refused("%s is ship %s of plan %s — rejoin it with --plan %s" % (pin_label(pin), other[1], other[0], other[0]))
        if helmlib.load_plan(pid) is None:
            # the plan is the yard's: made here, its skipper record the caller's, as `helm ship` would make it
            helmlib.new_plan(pid, name, manager={"session": laid.get("session"), "host": laid.get("host"), "harness": "wharf --yard"},
                             repo=key)
        copy = helmlib.plan_dir(pid) / ("blueprint-%s.md" % name)
        with helmlib.locked(pid):
            # The lease first, under the plan's lock, so a rejoin at a stale generation changes nothing.
            # Judged by this process's own environment: over ssh the yard's side is a plain shell (it
            # refuses a session of its own, and ssh carries none), so a sender's rejoin from another Mac
            # passes unless it names a --gen; on the yard, a session that does not hold the lease is refused.
            why = lease.fence(pid, "wharf apply --yard", given=a.gen)
            if why:
                raise Refused(why[len("refused: "):] if why.startswith("refused: ") else why, lease.REFUSED_EXIT)
            p = need(pid)
            rec = dict((p.get("blueprints") or {}).get(name) or {})
            if rec and pin_key(rec.get("pin")) != pin_key(pin):
                raise Refused("plan %s has a ship %s already (%s): this one is another plan's"
                              % (pid, name, pin_label(rec["pin"]) if rec.get("pin") else "unpinned, %s" % (rec.get("file") or "no file")))
            if rec.get("pin") and rec["pin"].get("digest") != pin["digest"]:
                raise Refused("%s is pinned in plan %s at digest %s, and origin reads %s: a re-pin is not built yet — "
                              "push the pinned text back, or lay a new ship" % (pin_label(pin), pid, rec["pin"]["digest"][:12], pin["digest"][:12]))
            if not rec:
                rec.update(pin=pin, laid_by=laid, merge=merge, file=str(copy.resolve()), main=str(main), rel=pin["rel"])
            elif merge["value"] == "no" and (rec.get("merge") or {}).get("value") != "no":
                rec["merge"] = merge   # a rejoin keeps the keel's record; it can only take the merge away
            if not copy.is_file() or copy.read_text() != text:
                copy.write_text(text)
            p.setdefault("blueprints", {})[name] = rec
            helmlib.save_plan(p)
            if lease.read(pid) is None:   # a new ship, or one laid before S4: the yard holds it, gen 0
                lease.write_yard(pid, scope, here, "laid by wharf apply --yard")
    finally:
        held.close()
    if not a.json:
        say("wharf apply --yard: %s pinned at %s into plan %s on %s (merge %s: %s)" % (pin_label(pin), d[:12], pid, here, merge["value"], merge["why"]))
    return apply_ship(pid, str(copy), as_json=a.json)


def yard_lease():
    """helm's leaselib, or Refused: --yard writes the ship's lease, and lays no ship it cannot fence."""
    if leaselib is None:
        raise Refused("helm's leaselib.py is not beside its helmlib.py (%s): --yard writes the ship's lease" % _HELMLIB.parent)
    return leaselib


def ship_ended(f, pid):
    """True once `wharf status <f> --json` — a fresh process, as the passes are — says the ship ended."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([str(HERE / "wharf"), "status", f, "--plan", pid, "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300)
        return bool(r.returncode == 0 and all(s.get("ended") for s in json.loads(r.stdout or "[]")) and r.stdout.strip() != "[]")
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return False


def cmd_watch(a):
    """`wharf apply --watch`: a pass over every ship named every --every minutes until each has
    ended, or the process is stopped. Each pass is `bin/wharf apply` run afresh, so a merge that
    renames or rewrites the yard's files (rename S5) never runs stale code here — this loop holds
    no state of its own beyond the file list. Attended only, as a start is; the tick stays as D5-A
    left it (disarmed). A pass's lines are printed only when it said something (--quiet: the
    tick's rule, a standing row said once)."""
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"):
        raise SystemExit("wharf apply --watch: attended only, as a start is (CLAUDE_UNATTENDED=%s)" % os.environ["CLAUDE_UNATTENDED"])
    if a.once or a.all or a.dry_run or a.json:
        raise SystemExit("wharf apply --watch: its passes are full applies; not with --once, --all, --dry-run or --json")
    if not a.files:
        raise SystemExit("wharf apply --watch: one or more blueprint files")
    for f in a.files:
        # each pass is a plain apply, which the fence would refuse every --every minutes: say it once
        why = yard_fence(load_blueprint(f, a.plan))
        if why:
            print("wharf apply --watch: refused: %s" % why, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    pid = plan_id(a.plan)
    files = [str(Path(f).resolve()) for f in a.files]
    sess = a.session or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID")
    extra = (["--launch", "--launches", str(a.launches)] + (["--session", sess] if sess else [])) if a.launch else []
    limit = int(os.environ.get("WHARF_WATCH_PASSES") or 0)   # tests: stop after this many passes
    n = 0
    while True:
        n += 1
        left = [f for f in files if not ship_ended(f, pid)]
        if not left:
            say("wharf apply --watch: every ship ended (%s) — done after %d pass%s" % (
                ", ".join(Path(f).name for f in files), n - 1, "" if n == 2 else "es"))
            return 0
        for f in left:
            exe = HERE / "wharf"
            if not exe.is_file():
                raise SystemExit("wharf apply --watch: %s is gone (renamed?): start the watch again from its new name" % exe)
            r = subprocess.run([str(exe), "apply", f, "--plan", pid, "--quiet"] + extra, capture_output=True, text=True)
            out = ((r.stdout or "") + (r.stderr or "")).rstrip()
            if out:
                say("— %s pass %d, %s%s" % (time.strftime("%H:%M"), n, Path(f).name, (" (exit %d)" % r.returncode) if r.returncode else ""))
                say(out)
        if limit and n >= limit:
            return 0
        time.sleep(max(0.0, a.every * 60))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- status

def cmd_orphans(a):
    """Orca repos and Runs that no plan on this Mac accounts for: what a scratch ship leaves behind.
    Orca 1.4.229 can remove neither (no `repo remove`, no run delete), so this only lists them; the
    first S1 probe's `yard-probe.9vWy` and `run_8910502da80f` are the first rows of the yard's. A Run
    is an orphan when no plan records it as a ship's `orca_run`; a repo when its folder is gone, or it
    is neither a registry repo (`<projects>/<name>`) nor a plan's. Reads only."""
    o = orca()
    if not o._app_up():
        print("wharf status: Orca is not running here (the app's runtime answers the CLI)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    runs_seen, repos_seen = set(), set()
    for pid in helmlib.list_plans():
        for rec in ((helmlib.load_plan(pid) or {}).get("blueprints") or {}).values():
            if rec.get("orca_run"):
                runs_seen.add(rec["orca_run"])
            if rec.get("main"):
                repos_seen.add(os.path.realpath(rec["main"]))
            f = blueprint_file(rec)
            if f:
                try:
                    repos_seen.add(os.path.realpath(str(ship_repo(load_recorded(pid, f), rec)[1])))
                except (blueprintlib.BlueprintError, OSError):
                    pass
    try:
        reg = (common.repos_json() and json.loads(common.repos_json().read_text()).get("repos")) or {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        print("wharf status: the registry is unreadable — every repo outside a plan is listed", file=sys.stderr)
        reg = {}
    for name in reg:
        repos_seen.add(os.path.realpath(str(common.PROJECTS / name)))
    out = {"runs": [], "repos": []}
    runs, cursor = [], None
    for _ in range(20):   # paged: --limit tops out at 100
        res, err = o._call(None, ["orchestration", "run-list", "--limit", "100"] + (["--cursor", cursor] if cursor else []), timeout=60)
        if err:
            print("wharf status: Orca unread — %s" % err, file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        runs += (res or {}).get("runs") or []
        cursor = (res or {}).get("nextCursor")
        if not cursor:
            break
    for r in runs:
        # Orca's own `legacy` row and `bin/harness run`'s Runs are no ship's leftovers
        if r.get("legacy") or str(r.get("objective") or "").endswith("(bin/harness run)"):
            continue
        if r.get("id") and r["id"] not in runs_seen:
            out["runs"].append({"run": r["id"], "objective": r.get("objective"), "created": r.get("created_at")})
    res, err = o._call(None, ["repo", "list"], timeout=60)
    if err:
        print("wharf status: Orca unread — %s" % err, file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    for r in (res or {}).get("repos") or []:
        path = r.get("path") or ""
        if not os.path.isdir(path):
            out["repos"].append({"repo": r.get("displayName") or path, "path": path, "why": "its folder is gone"})
        elif os.path.realpath(path) not in repos_seen:
            out["repos"].append({"repo": r.get("displayName") or path, "path": path, "why": "no plan and not a registry repo"})
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True))
        return 0
    for r in out["repos"]:
        say("repo %s — %s (%s)" % (r["repo"], r["path"], r["why"]))
    for r in out["runs"]:
        say("run  %s — %s (%s)" % (r["run"], r["objective"] or "no objective", r["created"] or "?"))
    say("%d repo(s) and %d Run(s) in Orca that no plan here accounts for; Orca can remove neither, so they are listed only"
        % (len(out["repos"]), len(out["runs"])))
    return 0


def cmd_status(a):
    if a.orphans:
        return cmd_orphans(a)
    pid = plan_id(a.plan)
    p = need(pid)
    recs = p.get("blueprints") or {}
    if a.what and a.what.endswith(".md"):
        names = [load_blueprint(a.what, pid)["name"]]
    else:
        names = [a.what] if a.what else sorted(recs)
    st = plan_status(pid)
    out = []
    for name in names:
        rec = recs.get(name)
        if not rec:
            raise SystemExit("wharf status: no ship %s in plan %s" % (name, pid))
        reads = None
        if rec.get("orca_run"):
            reads, why = orca_reads(rec["orca_run"], rec.get("coordinator"))
            if why:
                print("wharf status: Orca unread — %s" % why, file=sys.stderr)
        tasks = {t.get("id"): t for t in (reads or {}).get("tasks") or []}
        ws = {}
        for w in (reads or {}).get("workers") or []:
            ws.setdefault(w.get("taskId"), []).append(w)
        blocks = []
        bp = None
        if blueprint_file(rec):
            try:
                bp = load_recorded(pid, blueprint_file(rec))
            except blueprintlib.BlueprintError:
                bp = None
        ids = [s["id"] for s in bp["blocks"]] if bp else sorted(k for k, v in (p.get("tasks") or {}).items() if v.get("ship") == name)
        for sid in ids:
            t = (p.get("tasks") or {}).get(sid) or {}
            ot = tasks.get(t.get("orca_task")) or {}
            w = (ws.get(t.get("orca_task")) or [{}])[0]
            blocks.append({"id": sid, "plan": (st.get(sid) or {}).get("status") or "planned",
                           "progress": (st.get(sid) or {}).get("progress"), "orca_task": t.get("orca_task"),
                           "orca": ot.get("status"), "dispatch": w.get("dispatchId"), "dispatch_status": w.get("dispatchStatus")})
        out.append({"ship": name, "file": rec.get("file"), "run": rec.get("orca_run"), "coordinator": rec.get("coordinator"),
                    "digest": (rec.get("digest") or "")[:12], "blocks": blocks, "ended": rec.get("ended")})
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True))
        return 0
    for s in out:
        say("ship %s — Run %s, coordinator %s, digest %s" % (s["ship"], s["run"] or "none yet", s["coordinator"] or "—", s["digest"] or "—"))
        width = max([len(b["id"]) for b in s["blocks"]] + [1])
        for b in s["blocks"]:
            say("  %-*s  %-8s orca %-10s %s%s" % (width, b["id"], b["plan"], b["orca"] or "—",
                                                 ("dispatch %s %s" % (b["dispatch"], b["dispatch_status"] or "")) if b["dispatch"] else "",
                                                 ("  · " + b["progress"][:80]) if b["progress"] else ""))
    return 0


def ship_of_caller(pid, block, branch, repo=None):
    """(ship, blueprint) of the ship whose block `block` is, in plan `pid`'s recorded blueprints; None
    when the plan, or a block of that name in a blueprint of it, is not there. The caller's own record
    decides — the ship id and the block id wharf starts a session with (DISPATCH_SHIP or DISPATCH_PLAN, DISPATCH_TASK) —
    never a match of branch names across every plan on this Mac. The branch asked about must be the
    one the plan recorded for that block (wharf's seed of it): a block session that starts some other
    branch — a handoff, its own next stage — is not that block's successor and goes on as before.
    `repo`, when given, must be the blueprint's. A recorded blueprint that is gone or no longer loads is
    raised when nothing else matched: a guard that cannot read its ship must say so, not read as "not
    a ship"."""
    p = helmlib.load_plan(pid)
    if not p:
        if (helmlib.plan_dir(pid) / "plan.json").exists():   # there, but load_plan swallowed why
            raise ValueError("plan %s: plan.json does not parse" % pid)
        return None
    t = (p.get("tasks") or {}).get(block) or {}
    if not t.get("ship") or branch not in [b for b in (t.get("branch"), t.get("seeded_branch")) if b]:
        return None   # no ship's task by that id, or a branch the block was not started on
    broke = None
    for name, rec in sorted((p.get("blueprints") or {}).items()):
        if name != t["ship"]:
            continue
        f = blueprint_file(rec)
        if not f:
            broke = broke or "%s: recorded, not found" % (rec.get("file") or rec.get("rel") or name)
            continue
        try:
            bp = load_recorded(pid, f)
        except (blueprintlib.BlueprintError, OSError) as e:
            broke = broke or "%s: %s" % (f, e)
            continue
        if repo and ship_repo(bp, rec)[1].resolve() != Path(repo).resolve():
            continue
        if block in [st["id"] for st in bp["blocks"]]:
            return name, bp
    if broke:
        raise ValueError("plan %s records a blueprint that does not load (%s)" % (pid, broke))
    return None


def cmd_next(a):
    """Exit 0 and a line: the caller is a block of a ship and a block follows it (`wharf apply` starts
    that one). Exit 1, nothing printed: not a ship's block, or nothing follows it — the caller seeds as
    before. Exit 2, stderr: the check itself failed."""
    try:
        pid, block = helmlib.env("ship"), os.environ.get("DISPATCH_TASK")
        if not (pid and block):
            return 1   # a session that is not a block of a ship, or wharf's own start (a ship id, no block)
        hit = ship_of_caller(pid, block, a.branch, a.repo)
        if not hit:
            return 1
        name, bp = hit
        after = [s for s in bp["blocks"] if block in s["deps"]]
        if not after:
            return 1
        ids = [s["id"] for s in after]
        if a.json:
            print(json.dumps({"ship": name, "plan": pid, "block": block, "next": ids, "file": bp["path"]}, sort_keys=True))
            return 0
        say("%s is block %s of ship %s (plan %s): next is %s — `wharf apply` (the tick or the skipper) starts it, nothing is seeded here"
            % (a.branch, block, name, pid, ", ".join(s["id"] + ("" if s["kind"] == "block" else " (a decision)") for s in after)))
        return 0
    except Exception as e:   # an uncaught one would exit 1, which reads as "not a ship"
        print("wharf next: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2


def main(argv=None):
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="wharf", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    sp = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")
    s = sp.add_parser("check"); s.add_argument("file"); s.add_argument("--plan"); s.add_argument("--accept", action="store_true")
    s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    s = sp.add_parser("apply"); s.add_argument("files", nargs="*"); s.add_argument("--plan")
    s.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true"); s.add_argument("--once", action="store_true")
    s.add_argument("--all", action="store_true"); s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    s.add_argument("--watch", action="store_true"); s.add_argument("--every", type=float, default=5.0)
    s.add_argument("--launch", action="store_true")
    # --landings: the old name, read until rename S8 — a --watch loop started before S5 passes it to each pass
    s.add_argument("--launches", "--landings", dest="launches", type=int, default=2)
    s.add_argument("--session", help=argparse.SUPPRESS); s.add_argument("--quiet", action="store_true", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    s.add_argument("--yard", action="store_true"); s.add_argument("--no-merge", action="store_true")
    s.add_argument("--gen", type=int)   # the caller's lease generation (S4): fenced by plans/<id>/skipper.json
    s.add_argument("--pinned", help=argparse.SUPPRESS); s.add_argument("--laid-by", dest="laid_by", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    s = sp.add_parser("status"); s.add_argument("what", nargs="?"); s.add_argument("--plan"); s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    s.add_argument("--orphans", action="store_true")
    s = sp.add_parser("next"); s.add_argument("branch"); s.add_argument("--repo"); s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)
    fn = {"check": cmd_check, "apply": cmd_apply, "status": cmd_status, "next": cmd_next}.get(a.cmd)
    if not fn:
        ap.print_help()
        return 2
    try:
        return fn(a) or 0
    except (ValueError, FileNotFoundError) as e:
        raise SystemExit("wharf %s: %s" % (a.cmd, e))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
